window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101 The Hidden Certificate","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian barely made it through the doorway before his mother rushed past him, practically tripping over herself to beat him to the desk.","Luna Margaret snatched up the two folded certificates sitting on the mahogany surface and jammed them straight into her sleeve.","\"Mom. What are you hiding?\"","Alpha Sebastian closed the gap in three strides, nostrils flaring without him even meaning to. Something was off.","Luna Margaret’s stomach dropped. \"N-nothing. It’s nothing.\"","\"I saw it. And I can smell you’re lying.\" His eyes locked onto the awkward bulge poking out of her sleeve.","Luna Margaret’s face went white. \"You... you saw?!\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded slow. \"Why are you hiding it from me?\"","Her throat went tight. She swallowed hard. We are so screwed.","Alpha Roger had made it an order, not a request, Alpha Sebastian was not to catch wind of the dissolution paperwork. Not now, not while he was buried neck-deep in the biggest contract negotiation of his career.","She should’ve buried the damn thing in the pack vault. Anywhere but the study desk.","But how was she supposed to know her son would randomly need something from the study? He’d been grinding around the clock for weeks straight, barely answered a single family message.","\"What’s taking so long to grab our bond certificate?\" Alpha Roger’s voice cut through the tension as he strolled in, calm and heavy the way only an Alpha could manage.","He looked at his Luna. \"You find it?\"","Luna Margaret nodded so hard her neck hurt. \"Yeah! Got it right here.\"","\"Your bond certificate?\" Alpha Sebastian’s brow furrowed.","Luna Margaret’s heart skipped a beat. She rushed to her husband’s side, yanked the folded certificates out of her sleeve, pressed them into Alpha Roger’s hands like they were burning her fingers.","Alpha Roger took them without missing a beat, tucked them straight into his coat.","\"Why do you two suddenly need it?\" Alpha Sebastian’s eyes narrowed, suspicion creeping into his voice.","\"Your mother and I are marking thirty years since the bond ceremony.\" Alpha Roger’s tone stayed level, controlled. \"The Pack Elders are hosting something for it. Need the certificate on hand for the record.\"","Something in Alpha Sebastian’s gut prickled at that, the same instinct that had caught his mother red-handed thirty seconds ago. But he shoved it down.","His dad ran half the empire on instinct and always had a reason for everything, no point grilling him over a piece of paper.","\"Oh. Makes sense.\"","\"Quit overthinking things.\" Alpha Roger read him like a book, the way any Alpha could read the tension rolling off his own son. \"Your mother and I are solid. You and Isabella are the ones who need to stop snapping at each other where the whole pack can hear. Makes us look weak.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s voice went firm. \"I don’t want to hear Isabella say one more word about breaking the bond between me and Eira. Ever.\"","Luna Margaret opened her mouth to argue. Alpha Roger shut her down with one look, no words needed.","\"I’ll handle her myself,\" he told Alpha Sebastian. \"Don’t sweat it.\"","Keeping Alpha Sebastian’s head clear mattered more right now. Bid was less than a week out. Zero room for drama.","Alpha Sebastian trusted his old man, gave a short nod. Alpha Roger waved Luna Margaret out. Once the door clicked shut, he asked, \"Bid prep on track?\"","\"Yeah. On track.\"","Alpha Sebastian scanned the shelves, hunting for one book, the one Eira left in his car years back, her notes scrawled through the margins. That book was what pulled them together in the first place.","\"Serena says her grandfather’s putting in a word for you at the evaluation.\" Alpha Roger leaned against the desk. \"Once you land this, go thank Alpha Victor face to face. And Serena too.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s hand froze on a spine. \"She never mentioned that to me.\"","\"You’ve been buried. She’s cutting you slack.\"","Alpha Roger’s voice sharpened a notch. \"She backs you because she actually cares. Don’t take that for granted. Text her back once in a while. Won’t kill you.\"","Alpha Sebastian knew he’d been ghosting her. Every time he opened his phone to reply, the words just wouldn’t come.","Stuck. Torn between something he couldn’t even name.","Or maybe he just couldn’t face her anymore.","\"Deal’s all that matters right now,\" Alpha Sebastian said, mostly to himself. \"Rest can wait.\"","\"Career comes first, sure.\" Alpha Roger nodded. \"But don’t sleep on the people in your corner. Serena’s pulled a lot of weight for you.\"","\"Eira’s pulled weight too.\" Out before he could stop it.","Alpha Roger waved it off. \"Cooking dinner’s not exactly the same league.\"","Alpha Sebastian let it go, tucked the book under his arm. \"Heading out.\"","\"Go.\"","The second he was gone, Luna Margaret rushed back in. \"One more second and I would’ve cracked! Thought he actually saw them. Nearly gave me a heart attack.\"","\"Saw what?\" Isabella wandered in.","\"Grown-up stuff. Not your business,\" Alpha Roger said.","\"Fine.\" She pouted.","Alpha Roger turned on both of them, tone gone hard. \"Listen up. Nobody messes with Alpha Sebastian right now. Nobody stresses him out. Biggest deal of his career’s on the line. Hate Eira all you want, keep it locked up. We clear?\"","His eyes cut to Isabella. \"You especially. You never know when to shut it.\"","Her lip quivered. \"I know, okay?\"","--","On the drive back, Alpha Sebastian called Eira again.","\"You’re staying at Mrs. Thorne’s place tonight?\"","\"Need something?\" Eira stood by the floor-to-ceiling window in Lila’s sixty-sixth-floor suite, staring out at the city lights sprawled below.","\"I’ll swing by and pick you up.\"","\"It’s late. Don’t want to bother anyone.\" Her tone stayed flat. \"Got an early class tomorrow anyway. Easier if I just crash here. Aren’t you swamped right now?\"","\"I know. Sorry I’ve been so MIA lately.\"","\"You haven’t been.\"","You haven’t done anything wrong, she thought, cold.","\"We’ll celebrate once this deal’s done, right? Like we planned?\"","\"Yeah. Already got your gift sorted.\" Alpha Sebastian pictured the car he’d bought her, sleek, pricey, six figures. She’d love it. She had to.","Eira couldn’t care less about gifts.","\"Working at the office again tomorrow?\"","\"Yeah. Since you haven’t been home, I haven’t really gone back either.\" His voice went soft. \"Eira... I miss you.\"","\"Do you?\" Her voice came out cold, hollow, not a shred of warmth or belief in it. \"I’m exhausted. Going to bed.\"","\"Okay. Night.\"","Alpha Sebastian hung up. She still sounded distant. Probably still worked up over the whole Isabella thing.","Better to give her space.","He turned the car toward the office instead.","Back in the suite, Lila said, \"Gotta give the guy credit, he works hard.\"","Eira nodded. That drive, that ambition, that was part of what made her fall for him in the first place.","\"Too bad his character’s absolute trash,\" Lila added.","Eira grabbed her phone, texted Rachel: Starting tomorrow, no more hiding. Mask and hat can come off.","Rachel shot back instantly: Got it.","Eira looked up. \"Heading back to the house tomorrow. He’ll be out all weekend, so I’m grabbing my stuff then.\"","\"I’m coming with.\""]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102 Packing Up the Past","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, back at the office, Alpha Sebastian’s phone buzzed. A message from the head of the wellness clinic.","[Mr. Hale, we’re having a power outage over here, cameras are down. Want me to go snap a few photos of Mrs. Hale in class, just to keep you posted?]","Alpha Sebastian stared at the screen for a second, something twisting in his chest.","He typed out two words: [Sure.]","He stared at it. Deleted it.","[No need.]","[From now on, don’t bother.]","Eira was already dealing with enough right now. If she ever found out he’d had someone keeping tabs on her like this, snapping photos behind her back, it’d only make things worse between them.","He set the phone down.","He hadn’t even clocked it yet, this quiet shift in how he treated her. His whole set of priorities had rearranged itself without him noticing.","Back at the start, he’d been scared she’d slip out of his grip. That’s why he’d made her quit her job, no matter how much she pushed back.","Now? Her feelings came first. Before anything else.","When a guy starts putting someone else’s feelings ahead of his own agenda, that means something.","He liked her.","He just hadn’t figured that out yet.","--","Eira punched in the door code, stepped inside.","Stale air. Dust on the shoe cabinet. Nobody had set foot in here in weeks.","She glanced around the entryway. Four years of her life in this place, and it already felt like someone else’s apartment.","\"You taking all your shoes?\" Lila was already digging through the cabinet.","\"Just grab whatever’s mine.\" Eira headed into the bedroom, swept the last of her things into a bag, a couple sweaters, some odds and ends. Barely anything left. Two minutes, done.","Lila’s phone buzzed. She answered, listened, groaned. \"Professor Chase, I swear to god.\" Hung up. \"Eira, I gotta run, lab emergency. Got someone coming to help you haul this stuff though, don’t even argue.\"","\"It’s one bag, Lila. I don’t need backup.\"","\"Too late, he’s already on his way. Man’s got nothing else going on anyway.\" Lila grabbed her coat. \"When I’m back, we’re hitting my bar. Drinks on me.\"","\"You say that every time.\"","\"And I mean it every time.\" Lila winked and was out the door.","Eira stood there a second, bag slung over one shoulder. The living room caught her eye, dust sitting thick on every flat surface, the leather sofa dull with grime along the seams.","She set the bag down by the door. Told herself she’d just wipe the counters, a few minutes, tops.","--","Thirty minutes later, sweat beaded on Eira’s forehead as she knelt in front of the leather sofa, working a rag into the creases.","The doorbell rang. The door was already cracked open.","\"Who is it?\" She looked up, tense for a second.","[Please don’t be Sebastian.]","\"Me.\"","Alpha Killian stepped through the door. His eyes found her immediately, on her knees, soaked in sweat, rag in hand.","His jaw went tight.","He scanned the apartment. Three bedrooms, two baths. Cramped. Dated.","Alpha Sebastian pulled in seven figures a year and put her in this?","Money for his precious Serena. None for his own wife. And now, with things falling apart between them, she was still here scrubbing his floors.","Her clothes were filthy. Dust smudged across her face.","Alpha Killian crossed the room in four strides.","\"Alpha Killian.\" Eira wasn’t surprised to see him. Lila must’ve called him.","The two of them bickered nonstop, but when it mattered, they always showed up for each other.","\"Don’t Alpha Killian me.\" His voice came out sharp, controlled fury simmering just under it. He yanked the rag out of her hand, tossed it in the murky basin.","Dirty water splashed across the floor between them.","\"You enjoy this? Playing maid?\"","Eira opened her mouth to explain.","\"Ridiculous,\" he muttered. \"Come on. We’re leaving.\"","He grabbed her wrist.","She didn’t budge, eyes still on the unfinished work. \"Just need a few more minutes—\"","\"Forget it.\"","Alpha Killian’s patience snapped. He bent down, threw her over his shoulder like a sack of potatoes, turned for the door.","Eira gasped, grabbing his shoulder for balance. \"Alpha Killian!\"","\"Shut up.\"","He didn’t slow down. The driver was already waiting outside.","\"Grab those two bags.\" Alpha Killian nodded at the hallway. \"Careful with them.\"","\"Yes, Alpha Killian.\" The driver scooped them up, followed behind.","\"Alpha Killian, please, put me down.\" Eira kept her voice level despite how ridiculous this was, getting hauled around like luggage. She jostled when he adjusted his grip, on purpose, she was sure of it.","First time in her life a man had ever slung her over his shoulder like this. She was mortified and pissed in equal measure, though only her eyes gave away the second part.","No point fighting it. She knew that much.","\"At least let me finish,\" she said quietly. \"I lived there four years. I should leave it right.\"","\"Absolutely not.\"","The elevator dinged. She got carried in, carried out, carried through the lobby, finally dropped into the backseat of Alpha Killian’s car.","Before she could scramble for the other door, Alpha Killian slid in beside her, slammed it shut.","She reached for the handle.","He caught her wrist. Hard. Face like ice.","\"Try it. See what happens.\"","Weirdly, she wasn’t scared. Even staring down that look, she felt steady.","She just couldn’t figure out where all this anger was coming from.","They were employer and employee. Former employer and employee, technically. At most, he was her friend’s older brother.","She tugged against his grip. He didn’t let go.","\"This is my business, Alpha Killian.\""]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103 Nosebleed","paragraphs":["Something in Alpha Killian’s chest pulled tight. [Ungrateful.]","The driver tossed Eira’s two bags in the trunk, climbed in front. \"We heading out, Alpha Killian?\"","\"Drive,\" Alpha Killian said, flat.","\"Wait.\" Eira’s voice cut in at the exact same second, calm but firm.","The driver’s eyes flicked to the mirror, then just... stayed put. Not his fight.","Alpha Killian shot him a look anyway. \"I said drive.\"","The driver didn’t move. Eira gave him a small nod, thanks, then turned back to Alpha Killian, steady as ever. \"I lived in that place four years, Alpha Killian. Maybe you’ve never had to fight for somewhere to call your own. I have. I’m not walking out and leaving it trashed.\"","Something flickered across his face at that, the edges of it going soft for half a second.","\"Growing up, you don’t get to keep much of anything,\" she added. \"That apartment was mine, for a while. I want to leave it decent.\"","Her eyes didn’t waver. Clear straight through.","Alpha Killian felt that land somewhere he didn’t expect.","Still, he didn’t cave. He jerked his chin at the driver. \"Go handle it.\"","The driver started to climb out.","\"You don’t know the code,\" Eira said.","The driver froze halfway out of his seat, looked back at Alpha Killian, silently asking what now.","Alpha Killian sat there a beat, jaw working. Then he shoved the door open and got out himself.","\"Fine. Let’s go.\" He stood by the car, arms crossed, waiting.","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"Changed your mind fast.\"","\"Didn’t change anything. Just moving things along.\" He was already walking.","She rolled her eyes and jogged a step to catch up.","Back upstairs, Alpha Killian dropped onto the sofa like he owned the place, arms crossed, watching her dig a rag out from under the sink.","\"You’re really doing this,\" he muttered, half to himself.","Eira wiped the sofa down till it gleamed, scrubbed the shoe cabinet, swept the floor clean, bagged the trash, hauled it up with both hands.","\"Alpha Killian, done. We can go.\"","Alpha Killian let out a cold laugh. \"Not even one last look around?\"","She missed the edge in his voice completely. Shook her head. \"Nothing left to see once it’s clean.\"","His eyes dropped to the bag in her hands. He reached for it. She beat him to the elevator button instead.","Doors dinged open. \"Almost missed it,\" she murmured.","Alpha Killian gave up on taking the trash from her.","Floor numbers dropped. Felt like walking away from her old life one number at a time.","Hit the lobby. Her eyes stung, just a little. Corner of her mouth curved up anyway.","Alpha Killian caught both, the red rimming her eyes and the smile. Didn’t say a word.","--","Eira stood in front of the green dumpster outside, dropped the black bags in one by one. Peeled off her gloves, tossed those in too.","Her palms were red, slick with sweat.","A folded square of fabric showed up in front of her face.","She turned. Alpha Killian was holding out his pocket square.","\"That’s not for wiping sweat,\" she said. \"It’s decorative.\"","\"You know a lot about that, huh.\" Alpha Killian’s tone came out sharper than he meant.","He regretted it the second it left his mouth. He knew exactly where she’d picked that up, years of taking care of Alpha Sebastian.","Just thinking about that guy made his jaw clench.","\"Let’s go.\" His voice landed harder than he wanted it to.","Eira started walking, climbed back in the car. Alpha Killian followed.","Engine started up.","\"You’re a mess,\" Alpha Killian said, looking her over.","The driver handed back wet wipes without a word.","Alpha Killian grabbed her chin, held her still, started wiping her face down. Grip too tight.","She winced, tried to pull back.","\"Hold still.\" He kept going, her cheeks going pink from the rubbing.","\"Take a hint,\" he muttered. \"Quit saying yes to everyone who asks you for something.\"","Let go. Her jaw ached, skin stung, nothing broken.","She stared at him a beat. He let her.","Then pulled out her phone.","[Lila. New rule. Something this small happens again, don’t call your brother. Deal?]","Alpha Killian had been scowling since the moment he walked in.","Lila was elbow-deep in lab work. No reply.","--","Cleaning had worn Eira out. Her eyelids kept drooping, she’d blink them open, fight it a second, then they’d sink again. Her head dipped forward little by little.","Alpha Killian pressed a loose fist to his mouth, hiding the edge of a smile.","He kept her in his peripheral vision.","This time her eyes stayed shut. Out cold.","His voice dropped low. \"Slow down. Turn the heat up.\"","The driver eased off the gas, bumped the temp up to seventy-eight.","The car hit a speed bump, barely a jolt, but Alpha Killian’s eyes cut to the driver like a blade. The driver pretended not to notice.","Both of them checked on Eira. Still out. Deep asleep.","She must be running on empty.","A few minutes later, weight settled against Alpha Killian’s shoulder. Her head leaned into him, hair spilling across his chest, the ends brushing his hand.","He went rigid.","Only dared glance at her sideways. Hair covered half her face, but he could make out the bridge of her nose, the curve of her mouth through the strands.","His fingers twitched. Barely grazed the ends of her hair resting on his hand.","His expression went dark. Unreadable.","An hour later, the car pulled up outside 9 Southridge Estate Drive","The driver stepped out quiet, opened the door careful, shut it just as careful, then left.","Just the two of them now.","Alpha Killian didn’t move an inch.","Sun dipping low.","Eira stirred, eyes fluttering open. Driver’s seat, empty. She clocked her own position.","Head shot up.","Crack.","Skull straight into Alpha Killian’s nose.","She froze. [Oh no.]","Alpha Killian pressed his lips together, hand flying up to cover his nose. Eyes on her, half-lidded, unreadable.","\"I’m so sorry, Alpha Killian—\"","Then she saw it. Blood leaking between his fingers.","Her eyes went wide.","He felt it too, warm, steady, dripping.","Eira moved fast. \"Head down, not back. Tilt forward.\" She grabbed his wrist and pulled his hand away, pinched the bridge of his nose herself. \"I’m calling Dr. Wood.\"","Before Alpha Killian could even wonder how she had Barry’s number, she was already dialing.","\"Dr. Wood, Alpha Killian’s got a bloody nose. 9 Southridge Estate Drive.\"","Pinching alone wasn’t cutting it fast enough. Eira’s eyes swept the yard, landed on a scraggly patch of weeds growing along the fence line.","Yarrow. Feathery leaves, little white clusters. Old trick. Worth a shot.","She jogged over, pinched off a few sprigs, came back working them between her palms until they broke down into a rough green paste. Rolled two small plugs.","\"This is gonna feel weird for a second.\"","Alpha Killian eyed the tissue-sized green plugs like they were about to bite him.","Absolutely not.","His hand was already soaked in blood.","Eira didn’t care. Leaned in close, tugged at his wrist.","Didn’t budge.","She pulled again. Blood kept coming. Her patience snapped.","\"Killian.\"","Full name. No title. Voice dead firm.","Alpha Killian’s heart skipped."]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104 A New Address","paragraphs":["Barry Wood rolled up to 9 Southridge Estate Drive. Cut across the yard, grass grown out wild, nobody had touched a mower in weeks, and walked into the main hall.","Alpha Killian was sprawled on the sofa, head tipped back, chin up.","His eyes locked on Barry the second he walked in, gleaming with something downright dangerous.","Two green plugs jammed up his nostrils.","Barry’s stomach dropped. [ Who in the world stuffed weeds up the Grim Reaper’s nose?]","\"Alpha Killian, you run into something? Or did something run into you?\"","Alpha Killian’s stare turned sharp enough to cut glass.","Barry clammed up fast. Took a step closer, blinked hard. \"Who stuck yarrow up there?\"","Sure as hell wasn’t Alpha Killian’s idea.","\"Dr. Wood.\" Eira walked out of the kitchen carrying a kettle, worry written all over her face.","Barry clocked her and it clicked instantly. He grinned. \"Miss Crawford played field medic, huh?\"","Eira nodded. \"Dr. Wood, just Eira’s fine. I don’t work for Alpha Killian anymore.\"","Barry blinked. [What in the hell happened here?]","Wasn’t touching that with a ten-foot pole. Whatever was going on between these two, none of his business.","He dialed his tone back a notch. \"Miss Crawford, then.\"","\"Yarrow, that’s an old-school trick,\" Barry said, snapping on gloves, grabbing his tweezers. \"Actually works pretty well for bleeding. Folks used to yank it off the roadside, chew it up, slap it on a cut. Soldiers used it on the battlefield way back, that’s the real deal.\"","\"Wolves heal faster than regular folks anyway,\" he added, easing the plugs loose. \"This just gives it a head start. Give it an hour, you won’t even remember getting clocked.\"","He pulled the two green plugs out of Alpha Killian’s nose.","Alpha Killian’s nostrils flared once, catching the sharp green bite of the herb still clinging to his skin, way stronger than any human nose would’ve picked up. His eyes cut to Eira. \"This the same stuff you used to pick as a kid?\"","Surprise flashed across her face. He actually remembered that?","She’d only mentioned it once, in passing. And he’d filed it away like it mattered.","\"Yeah,\" she murmured, eyes still on his nose.","--","Bleeding had stopped.","Barry wiped the dried blood off Alpha Killian’s face. The stain on his collar, though, that had already set in for good.","Shirt’s a goner. Guess I’m buying the man a new one.","\"What size shirt you wear, Alpha Killian?\" Eira asked.","Alpha Killian glanced down at his own collar, noticed the blood too. Didn’t matter much, he had a closet full of shirts back home.","Eira sized him up for a second, doing quick math in her head. Guy’s six-three, built like that, probably a 44 or 46 jacket. Neck’s gotta be a seventeen, seventeen-and-a-half.","\"Seventeen?\" she guessed.","\"Seventeen and a half,\" Alpha Killian said, flat.","Seventeen was your average guy who skipped leg day.","Seventeen and a half meant he actually put in the work.","His eyes darkened a shade.","Eira missed the chip on his shoulder completely. Just nodded, filed it away, made a mental note to grab him a bigger size.","Barry wrapped up the cleanup. Eira handed Alpha Killian a cup of hot water.","He glanced in the cup. No ginger tea in it, the stuff she always kept around for herself.","Figures. Hoarding the good stuff.","He took a sip anyway.","Eira poured a second cup, passed it to Barry.","Barry lifted it to his mouth.","Alpha Killian’s voice sliced through like a whip. \"When’d you two swap numbers?\"","Barry froze, cup halfway to his lips. [Oh, here we go.]","Question wasn’t really for him. It was a shot across his bow.","[Dr. Wood?]","Alpha Killian never called him that. Normally it was \"Barry, get your ass over here\" or \"Barry, now\" or just \"Barry, move,\" always followed by an address and zero please-or-thank-you.","First time in his life this guy had ever talked to him like a functioning adult with manners. That alone told Barry everything he needed to know about how much trouble he was in.","Eira answered easy. \"Last time, at the clinic.\"","Barry jumped in fast. \"Miss Crawford used to work for Alpha Killian. I’m his doctor. We swapped numbers so I could actually reach him when he does something stupid. That’s the whole story.\"","First half sounded professional enough. Second half sounded weird as hell.","Eira caught the odd phrasing but let it slide.","\"Alpha Killian, Dr. Wood, sit tight. I need to grab some stuff from outside.\"","Barry figured that was that. Lifted his cup, headed for the sofa. Butt halfway down when-","\"Trunk. Two bags.\"","Barry froze mid-sit.","[You gotta be kidding me.","I’m your doctor, not your bellhop. Twenty years of friendship and you still treat me like the help.]","Eira jumped in fast. \"You don’t need to bother Dr. Wood. I can grab them myself.\"","Barry’s eyes lit up. Grinned. \"Miss Crawford, let’s go together. Two hands beat one, and honestly, I could use the excuse to get out of doing manual labor solo.\"","\"Thanks,\" Eira said.","Both of them turned for the door.","The Reaper’s voice cut in behind them. \"Stop.\"","They turned back. Eira looked confused. Barry looked like he was enjoying this way too much.","\"Barry gets the bags.\" Alpha Killian waved Eira toward the sofa.","Eira shook her head. \"I’ll get them.\"","Barry kept grinning, arms crossed now, clearly not moving an inch on his own.","Alpha Killian gave up, straightened his shirt, stood. Shot Barry a look that could strip paint off a wall. \"You. Sit. Drink your water.\"","\"Copy that, Alpha Killian.\" Barry dropped back down, thoroughly pleased with himself, finally getting a real sip in while he watched the two of them head outside.","--","Alpha Killian popped the trunk.","Eira bent to grab a bag. He beat her to it, fingers brushing hers.","She looked up. Got nothing but his jaw, set hard.","\"I got it,\" he said.","He slung both bags over his shoulder, bulky and awkward, and still walked like he owned the sidewalk.","Barry watched from the doorway, shaking his head. \"Golden spoon in his mouth his whole life, and here he is hauling luggage like a bellhop. Never thought I’d see the day.\"","Back inside, Eira reached for the bags. \"I can take it from here, Alpha Killian.\"","He handed them over. Held on a beat too long before letting go.","\"Thanks for everything. I’ve got stuff to sort out, so I won’t keep you two for dinner.\"","Translation: give me space. Alpha Killian got the hint.","He nodded at Barry. They left.","Barry hopped in the driver’s seat. \"Where’s your usual guy?\"","\"Sent him home.\"","Barry followed his gaze, locked on the open door, on Eira’s shape moving inside. \"Dude. You’re staring like a creep.\"","Alpha Killian didn’t answer.","\"At least wait till the divorce is final before you go full stalker.\"","\"Already final.\"","Barry’s eyebrows shot up. \"Wait, that’s it? Two bags, that’s everything she owns?\"","Alpha Killian nodded.","Barry let out a low whistle. \"Usually the woman walks off with half the furniture. Guy’s place looks like a crime scene after. But Sebastian Hale’s house? Probably looks exactly the same as it always did.\"","Actually, it didn’t. Small changes. Subtle ones.","But knowing Alpha Sebastian, he’d probably never even notice.","The thought irritated Alpha Killian. He pulled out his phone, fired off a message to Miles.","[Keep all the intel on Alpha Sebastian and Serena. Bring it to the bid meeting.]"]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105 A Request to Step Aside","paragraphs":["Sunday night, Alpha Sebastian came home.","He opened the door. Apartment was spotless. Clean, organized, back to how it used to be.","His face lit up. She’s back.","Lights were off. Must be asleep.","He moved quiet through the hall, pushed open the bedroom door, didn’t bother with the overhead light. Knew the layout by heart. Made his way to the nightstand, clicked on the lamp.","Warm yellow light spilled across the room.","Alpha Sebastian smiled, looked toward the bed.","Flat. No small shape curled under the blankets.","Comforter smooth. Perfectly made.","His smile died.","She’d been here. Then she’d left.","He sat on the edge of the bed, flipped on the main light, pulled out his phone, dialed.","Call connected. Then she hung up.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the screen, stunned.","His phone buzzed. A text.","Eira: [What is it?]","Sebastian: [You came back. Why’d you leave again?]","Eira: [Thought you weren’t coming home till next week.]","She meant it straight. Genuinely surprised he’d bothered making time to come home at all.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the reply. Every word felt like an accusation. A quiet reminder of how little time he actually spent there.","He typed back fast.","Sebastian: [I’m not avoiding home. I’m working for us. For our future.]","Eira: [I know.]","Two words. Landed like a punch. His jaw tightened. Sounded resentful. Bitter, even.","His temper flared, then crashed just as fast.","Wait.","She wasn’t the one who’d been gone all the time. He was the one who never showed up.","Alpha Sebastian shook his head, forced the anger back down.","Sebastian: [Once this week’s done, I won’t leave you alone anymore.]","The thought tugged at something in him. Mouth curved slightly. Warmth spread through his chest.","Later that night, Alpha Sebastian got in the shower.","Closed his eyes. Let the hot water run down his back.","Eira crossed his mind, out of nowhere.","His breath caught.","A second later, his body reacted. Fast. Hard.","He braced one hand against the tile, let it happen.","When it was done, he stared at his own hand, kind of stunned.","When did she start getting to me like this?","Ethan’s voice popped into his head. \"You’re seriously telling me you don’t feel anything for her?\"","Alpha Sebastian stood there, water running over his shoulders, pressed a hand to his chest.","Do I?","Do I actually like her?","No clue.","He stepped out, reached for his toothbrush. Cup was empty.","Frowned, opened the mirror cabinet himself, started digging around. Found a spare toothbrush shoved in the back, still sealed, and a half-used tube of toothpaste next to it.","Grabbed both. Then his hand froze.","Next to them, two plain silver bands.","Their rings.","Something in his chest went tight.","Then it hit him. Day Serena flew back into town, he’d taken his ring off before picking her up, left it on the nightstand.","Eira must’ve moved it in here at some point.","Her ring sat right next to his. She’d taken hers off too, probably doing chores, didn’t want to lose it down a drain or something.","He picked up both rings. Slid his own back on his left hand. Pocketed hers, tucked it into his wallet, careful.","[I’ll put it back on her when I see her.]","--","Three Days Until the Bid Meeting","The whole tech sector was in overdrive. Every company with skin in the Sovereign Processor Initiative was running final checks, polishing pitches, rehearsing like their lives depended on it.","At the National Institute, the team was just as slammed, gearing up for the bid opening and the signing right after. Results in the morning. Ink on paper by afternoon.","Dr. Victor Winthrop called Professor Davies into his office. Ran through a few logistics questions, nothing important, then eased into the real topic.","\"Serena’s been a piece of work lately. I know she’s given your team headaches.\" He folded his hands on the desk. \"She’s home now, grinding on her thesis, laying low. Do me a favor and don’t hold it against her.\"","Professor Davies read between the lines instantly. Kid’s grounded. Crisis averted.","Dr. Victor Winthrop wasn’t dumb. He knew exactly when to yank his granddaughter’s leash.","\"She’s young,\" Professor Davies said, smooth as ever. \"Passionate. You don’t see that much anymore.\"","He knew this wasn’t about logistics. Dr. Victor Winthrop hadn’t dragged him in here to talk schedules, an assistant could’ve handled that over email. This was something else.","\"Professor Davies.\" Dr. Victor Winthrop’s tone stayed light, but every word landed with weight. \"The signing. You and Miss Crawford are running point, correct?\"","And there it was.","Professor Davies kept his poker face on lock, brain already sprinting. He’s angling to get Serena in the room.","Lucky for him, he and Eira had seen this coming.","\"Everyone who put work into this project will be there for the signing, Dr. Victor Winthrop. Serena included.\"","Dr. Victor Winthrop’s eyes narrowed just a hair. Not falling for that.","Standing in a room and actually repping the project up front were two completely different animals.","\"Miss Crawford’s the lead engineer. She’s the one signing. You’re her advisor, you’ll be up there next to her.\" Beat. \"Professor Davies, make room for Serena. Put her front and center.\"","Professor Davies kept the smile plastered on. His gut was doing backflips.","Make room, my ass.","National contracts ran on strict protocol, three to five reps a side, no exceptions. Eira signs. Professor Davies stands beside her as her advisor. One more senior Institute official reps the department, has to show up no matter how hands-off they usually are.","Dr. Victor Winthrop wasn’t even the direct head of this project. Assigned Serena to the team, sure, then backed off completely. Didn’t matter. Guy’s rank alone cast a shadow over the whole building. The actual department head had been perfectly happy letting Eira run point and staying invisible. But ceremony day? Protocol says show up, no excuses.","That’s three slots, gone.","Fourth went to the lead engineer’s right hand, Claire, standing behind Eira, passing paperwork when needed.","Fifth was a toss-in. Optional. Nobody cared if that seat stayed empty.","Shove Serena into slot five, and she’s standing in the back, basically furniture.","Dr. Victor Winthrop wasn’t playing for furniture. He wanted her in Professor Davies’s seat.","This isn’t mentorship. This is a straight-up swap.","Professor Davies’s mind raced. He wasn’t handing over his spot without a fight. But telling a guy at Dr. Victor Winthrop’s level \"no\" to his face wasn’t exactly a walk in the park either.","Knock at the door saved him from answering.","\"Come in,\" Dr. Victor Winthrop called.","Door swung open. Eira walked in.","The second Claire tipped her off that Dr. Victor Winthrop had pulled Professor Davies into his office, she knew something was up. Came straight over.","One look at Professor Davies’s face told her everything.","\"Dr. Victor Winthrop.\" Cool as anything. \"I need Professor Davies. Something came up with the project data.\"","Professor Davies caught the cue instantly, stood up fast. \"Right. Let’s move.\"","They turned for the door.","\"Professor Davies.\"","Dr. Victor Winthrop’s voice stopped them cold.","\"Think about what I said.\"","Professor Davies’s spine locked up. He kept walking anyway, Eira right beside him."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106 The Background Check","paragraphs":["Eira shut the lab door behind them.","\"Data’s clean,\" she said. \"Nothing missing.\"","Davies gave her a look, half-impressed, half-spooked. \"Since when do you lie that well?\"","\"Since last month. Lots of practice.\"","Claire rushed over. \"Professor, what’d Dr. Victor Winthrop want?\"","Davies opened his mouth to dodge it.","\"It’s about Serena,\" Eira cut in. \"And the signing ceremony.\"","Davies blinked.","\"She’s been telling Sebastian she’s running this project. No spotlight at the ceremony, her whole story falls apart.\" Eira crossed her arms. \"And she’s been using this project to pump up her resume from day one.\"","\"You’re right,\" Davies muttered.","Claire’s jaw dropped. \"She’s been talking about the project? She signed an NDA!\"","\"Kept it vague. Just enough to dodge the fine print.\"","\"Classic,\" Davies said. \"Half a dozen projects in this field she could be hinting at. Nobody can pin her down.\"","\"That’s such crap,\" Claire snapped.","\"You say yes to him?\" Eira asked.","\"Not yet. He’s waiting.\"","Claire frowned. \"Yes to what?\"","\"Later.\" Eira turned to Davies, dead serious.","\"Say yes.\"","He stared at her.","\"Tell him no, he’ll make your life hell. Just play ball for now.\" She headed for the door. \"I’ve got this handled.\"","--","Davies sat on the request all evening, didn’t cave until right before bed. Made the yes look a lot more genuine.","Alpha Victor set his phone down, turned to a staff member. \"How’s Serena been?\"","\"Mostly holed up in her room or the study, Alpha. Only comes out to eat.\" The woman kept her eyes down, chin tucked, the posture settling into her shoulders before she’d even finished the sentence.","\"Not even the garden?\" He frowned.","She shook her head, caught the edge in his voice and swallowed against it, throat working once.","\"Where is she now?\"","\"Her room, Alpha.\"","He headed upstairs, knocked.","Inside, Serena was on the phone. \"Who is it?\"","\"Me.\" Alpha Victor’s voice cut through the door, no mistaking it.","She didn’t open up right away. \"Grandpa’s here. Call you back.\" Voice went soft. \"Love you, Seb. Talk soon.\"","Hung up, crossed the room, opened the door, pout locked and loaded.","\"Still sulking?\"","\"Wouldn’t dare be mad at you, Grandpa.\" Just enough spoiled-favorite-grandkid sass to sell it. Alpha Victor didn’t blink. Raised her himself. Knew the act by heart.","She stepped aside, let him in.","He scanned the mess. Clothes everywhere. Books dumped across the desk. \"A grown woman ought to keep her room together.\"","Serena scooped an armful of clothes, dumped them on a maid standing nearby.","The maid caught them without a word, dropped her gaze, and got to work fast, spine curved just slightly, careful never to turn her back fully on either of them.","Alpha Victor turned on her. \"Why isn’t anyone cleaning in here?\"","The maid’s hands stilled for half a second, scent of nerves sharp enough that even Serena caught it from across the room.","Whole house knew the rule: Serena was untouchable. Nobody wanted to be the one who screwed that up.","Not that they refused. She just never opened the door. Nobody was breaking it down.","\"Grandpa, I told them to stay out,\" Serena said fast. \"Not their fault.\"","He let it slide. The maid’s shoulders dropped an inch, breath easing out slow through her nose. Thank God the girl wasn’t the type to sell people out.","Serena caught her grandfather’s look, knew something was coming. Waved the staff off, shut the door.","\"What’s up? It’s late.\"","\"The bid meeting. Professor Davies caved.\"","\"Seriously?\" Her eyes lit up, a flicker of gold cutting through before settling back to brown. \"He’s handing me his spot?\"","She knew exactly what that meant. Standing where Davies stood, that’s a career-launcher. Especially at her age.","But her age was exactly the problem.","\"Grandpa, what if someone asks questions? Press is covering the signing.\"","He waved it off. \"Professor Davies already has the story straight. Says you’re a rising star, time to give young talent the stage. Guy’s built his whole reputation on mentoring. Fits him like a glove.\"","\"He said that? Exact words?\"","\"Yes. And listen.\" He kept going. \"You’ve got the résumé. Published papers, projects overseas. Anyone pushes back, that’s your answer. Nothing shady here. I’m good, not a magician. No skills, no spot, simple as that. Someone digs too deep, I’m the one holding the bag too.\"","She smiled, closed the distance. \"Thanks, Grandpa. Always got my back.\"","\"Then quit moping like I did you dirty.\"","\"Wasn’t moping.\" She hooked her arm through his, gave it a shake, same trick she’d pulled since she was five. Still worked every time. His stern face cracked, softened right up.","\"That was the Sebastian kid on the phone just now, wasn’t it?\"","\"Yeah.\" Serena nodded, cheeks going pink, pulse ticking up loud enough he didn’t need to ask twice.","Alpha Victor studied her for a second, curious about what kind of man could keep his granddaughter’s attention for so long.","\"Four years abroad, and he waited around the whole time?\"","\"He did. Flew out every year for my birthday too. Never told you.\" Serena bit her lip. \"Didn’t want you thinking I was distracted, not focused on my work. Sebastian kept his distance too, didn’t blow up my phone. But whenever I needed him, he showed up. Every single time.\"","Alpha Victor nodded slow, something like approval flickering across his face.","\"And in those four years, he didn’t get tangled up with anyone else?\"","Serena froze for half a beat.","Then shook her head, firm. \"No way. Sebastian wouldn’t look twice at anyone else.\" She paused. \"He told me if he ever has kids, he only wants them with me.\"","Alpha Victor’s eyebrows shot up. \"You two aren’t even married. Haven’t met each other’s families properly. And you’re already talking kids?\"","He frowned, clearly not thrilled with the idea.","Serena, meanwhile, had a totally different take. She’d actually been running the math on this for a while. Get pregnant, and Sebastian marries her. She’d bet money on it.","Guy was responsible to a fault. Part of why he’d dragged his feet on the divorce, as far as she knew, was some guilt trip about not wanting to just cut Eira loose.","But a baby changes everything.","They hadn’t used protection last time. Almost a month now. If her period didn’t show in the next few days, she’d swing by the hospital, get it confirmed."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107 The Ring in His Wallet","paragraphs":["\"Serena.\" Alpha Victor’s voice snapped her out of it.","She blinked. \"Sorry, Grandpa. Zoned out thinking about Seb.\"","He sighed. \"You promised you’d help him out. Guy’s ambitious, works hard. This project’s a big deal for him.\"","\"I know.\"","His tone softened, even if his face stayed stern. \"Quit worrying so much about him.\"","\"He’s not just ’him.’\" Serena grinned. \"He’s gonna be your grandson-in-law someday.\"","\"Watch it.\" No real heat behind it. Then his voice went serious. \"Listen up. Ceremony day, keep it simple. Nothing flashy. No designer stuff. No fancy bag. Got it?\"","He said it twice, just to make sure it stuck.","Serena nodded fast. She knew what was riding on this. \"Got it, Grandpa. Low-key, I promise.\"","\"Good.\"","\"But Grandpa,\" she brightened, \"can I run out tomorrow? Just to grab something to wear?\"","His eyes narrowed. He didn’t trust her to stay out of trouble for five minutes.","\"No. You stay put till the ceremony. We go together.\"","Her face fell. \"But I haven’t seen Sebastian in forever.\"","\"Sebastian this, Sebastian that, that’s all I hear out of you,\" he snapped. \"Go read a paper or something.\"","Serena wisely kept her mouth shut.","\"Fine. Whatever you say.\"","\"Good.\"","Alpha Victor got up, left the room. Once he was clear of the door, he called for the head of household staff.","\"Dig up everything you can on Alpha Sebastian Hale. I want to know if he’s been messing around with anyone else these past four years.\"","--","The day before the bid meeting, Alpha Sebastian knew he had to get home early. Recharge, reset, show up tomorrow sharp.","He pushed the front door open, found it already ajar. Something cooking, the smell drifting faint into the hallway.","\"Eira? You home?\"","He stepped in, scanned the room on instinct the way any Alpha would. His parents and sister sat on the living room sofa. He paused, eyes cutting toward the kitchen.","A heavyset figure moved around the stove. The housekeeper. Not Eira.","His mother caught the flash of disappointment cross his face before he could smooth it over, caught the way his shoulders dropped half an inch.","She bit back a sigh. Tomorrow mattered too much.","They needed him steady, confident, nothing pulling at him.","\"Seb, honey, come sit. Want a drink? Beer’s in the fridge. Dinner’s almost up.\"","\"Dad. Mom. Isabella.\" He nodded at each one, slipped off his coat, hung it by the door. \"Let me change first.\"","\"Go on.\"","Alpha Roger watched his son head down the hall, then turned sharp on his daughter, voice dropping low enough it wouldn’t carry past the room. \"Listen, Isabella. Don’t say or do anything tonight that upsets your brother. Understood?\"","Isabella rolled her eyes, popped a grape in her mouth. \"So I can’t mention Eira? Fine. Not much to say anyway. Place was spotless when she left. Looked like she was packing up for good.\"","Alpha Roger’s voice dropped further, barely a growl under the words. \"Don’t bring her up at all.\"","\"Fine. Whatever.\" She shrugged, chewing. \"Not like I want to talk about her. Makes me sick just thinking about it.\"","Alpha Sebastian came back in a gray henley, lounge pants.","Luna Margaret elbowed her daughter, sharp, a silent order to zip it.","Isabella caught her mother’s scent shift, that faint edge of warning that came off her when she meant business, and shoved another grape in her mouth instead of arguing.","Alpha Sebastian dropped onto the couch, pulled out his phone. Whole family here tonight. Didn’t feel right leaving Eira out, especially tonight of all nights.","Usually, the night before something big, she’d cook something special. Just the two of them, quiet, low-key.","Tonight, nothing. Just somebody else’s hands in the kitchen and a smell that wasn’t hers.","Alpha Roger caught him about to dial, cut in smooth. \"We already called her when we got here. She said she’s tied up tonight. Can’t make it.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"You called her?\"","\"I did. Not your mother. Not your sister.\"","Alpha Roger said it on purpose, watched his son’s face for the flicker he knew was coming.","Alpha Sebastian eased up a little. His dad, at least, knew how to keep things civil, knew better than to let his temper loose on Eira.","[She’d quit her job, right? So what could possibly keep her from a family dinner tonight?]","\"Why are you wearing that again?\" Alpha Roger’s voice cut through his thoughts.","Alpha Sebastian glanced down. \"What?\"","\"The ring.\" Alpha Roger nodded at his son’s left hand. \"Weren’t wearing it a few weeks back.\"","Alpha Sebastian lifted his hand, studied the band.","His face softened, the tension in his jaw easing out. \"My wedding ring. Mine and Eira’s.\"","Alpha Roger knew that already. What he didn’t know anymore was what the hell was going on in his son’s head.","One minute Alpha Sebastian’s saying the marriage had to end for his career, for the pack’s standing.","Next minute he’s slipping the ring back on like it still means something, like four years of history hadn’t just been signed away.","Bad timing, all of it. Tomorrow, Alpha Victor Winthrop would be in that room, Serena’s grandfather, head of a pack that outranked theirs on paper and never let anybody forget it.","A man like that catches even a whiff of his granddaughter tangled up with someone who couldn’t fully let go of an old marriage, ring and all, that’s the kind of thing that gets talked about at every gathering for years.","Hale Pack couldn’t afford that, not with everything riding on tomorrow.","\"Fine to wear it around the house,\" Alpha Roger said, careful, watching his son’s face. \"Tomorrow, at the ceremony? Not a good look. Don’t slip up on something that small.\"","Alpha Sebastian got it right away, read it straight off his father’s face, off the tightness around his eyes.","Looked down at the ring again.","\"Take it off tonight,\" Alpha Roger pushed. \"Won’t have to scramble in the morning. God forbid you drop it somewhere and lose it.\"","That last part landed harder than the rest. Alpha Sebastian let out a slow breath and slid the ring off.","Opened his wallet, tucked it in carefully, right next to another ring already sitting in the clear pocket.","Two rings, side by side, tucked into the same worn leather pocket.","His mouth curved slightly. Whole face went soft in a way it hadn’t all evening.","Alpha Roger glanced at the wallet, frowned. \"Why do you have Eira’s ring too?\"","The question had an edge to it. [She already took hers off. Why’s he still hanging on?]","\"She’s always careful with it,\" Alpha Sebastian said, quiet. \"Takes it off when she’s cleaning or cooking so it doesn’t get scratched up. Must’ve forgotten to put it back on this time. Didn’t want her losing it, so I’m holding onto it.\"","Tucked the wallet back in his pocket.","Dinner was already laid out. The family sat down together.","Alpha Sebastian snapped a photo of the spread, sent it to Eira.","[Dad said you’re busy tonight and can’t make it. What’s going on?]","No reply."]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108 Uninvited","paragraphs":["At that very moment, Eira sat at the dining table over at Number Nine Southridge Estates, a totally different crowd around her.","Beatrice Thorne. Martin. Professor Davies and his wife. Claire.","Table was loud. Good kind of loud.","Somebody clinked a fork against a glass, and for a second the noise dipped, just enough for Beatrice’s voice to slip through.","\"Alaric would’ve loved this,\" she said, eyes going a little glassy. \"Bet he’s up there somewhere, grinning like an idiot.\"","Davies’s wife laughed, wiped at her eyes with the back of her hand.","\"God, if this guy finally takes a weekend off because of it, I’ll throw a damn parade.\" She nudged her husband. \"Don’t get used to it.\"","\"Hey, this isn’t retirement, it’s a partnership,\" Davies shot back, grinning. \"Still got work to do.\" He squeezed her hand. \"Thanks, though. For putting up with me all these years.\"","\"Proud of you,\" she said, simple, and dropped a piece of roasted broccoli on his plate like that settled it.","Claire piped up. \"After tomorrow I’m finally telling my parents what I actually do for a living. They think I’m in some cult. Cops had to show up at their door and tell them to knock it off with the questions.\"","Table cracked up.","Then everyone’s eyes landed on Eira at once.","She stayed calm. \"Gonna go practice my signature a few more times tonight.\"","Beat. Then more laughing.","\"And tomorrow?\" Beatrice asked.","\"Tomorrow we get it done.\" Eira shrugged. \"Then we keep going. Bigger stuff.\"","Davies leaned in. \"Just this one project?\"","She shook her head. \"Nope. Not even close.\"","Nobody pushed for details. Whatever she was cooking up, that was enough for now.","\"To tomorrow,\" Davies said, lifting his glass of sparkling juice. \"And to you not getting poisoned. I know the Institute’s got you covered, but seriously, watch what you eat and drink.\"","\"I know.\" Eira’s voice went soft.","\"I’ll be fine. Serena’s laying low. And him,\" she didn’t bother with the name, \"he’s not getting under my skin anymore.\"","Beatrice and Davies both knew exactly who \"him\" meant.","Davies’s wife and Claire let it go, kept eating, the whole table easy again.","Then. Ding-dong.","\"Who’s showing up this late?\" Beatrice frowned. \"Anyone else know you’re staying here?\"","Eira thought about it. \"Maybe Lila.\"","Beatrice relaxed. \"The Sterling girl, that’s fine. Long as it’s not her brother, she can’t put it together.\"","\"I’ll check.\"","Eira got up, glanced at the security screen by the door.","Stomach dropped straight through the floor.","Hands in his pockets. Face giving away nothing.","Alpha Killian Sterling.","--","Across the table, Claire’s eyes kept darting between the two of them. Painfully obvious she was trying to figure out what these two actually were to each other.","Even if Eira hadn’t quit, it still seemed weird for her boss to show up at her house unannounced. Right?","But Claire didn’t dare ask.","Davies’s wife had no such hang-ups. She smiled warm, said what everybody at the table was already thinking.","\"Mr. Sterling, Eira doesn’t work for you anymore. And yet here you are. Still keeping in touch, huh?\"","Question landed clean, no wiggle room.","Alpha Killian took his time answering, in no hurry at all, like the question wasn’t even worth rushing for. Not many people managed to catch him off guard like that.","Eira didn’t miss a step.","\"I owe the guy. Big time. Three times over, actually.\"","Everyone looked at her.","She shrugged. \"Saved my life once. That’s one. Then there was this whole thing where he protected something I cared about a lot, don’t wanna get into it. That’s two.\" She paused, thinking back. \"And he kept me out of a mess I really didn’t want to be in. That’s three.\"","Claire’s eyes went wide. She leaned in, whispered, though not quiet enough. \"Okay, three life debts. That’s like, movie-villain-turned-good-guy territory. What, are you supposed to be his loyal sidekick for life now or something?\"","Eira froze, mouth half open, no comeback ready for that one.","Claire kept going, grin spreading. \"Or is this a ’my hero, take me, I’m yours’ kind of deal?\"","Eira reached over, flicked her on the forehead. \"Drop it.\"","Truth was, she should’ve settled one of those debts already. Had a whole plan for it. Then Sebastian showed up out of nowhere that same night, demanding to know where she was and what she was up to.","Of course it had to be that night.","Now she had zero idea how to pay Alpha Killian back. Not for any of it.","But Alpha Killian’s hearing was annoyingly good, and he’d caught every word Claire whispered.","He leaned back in his chair, unhurried, one arm draped over the back of it like he owned the room. Mouth curved up slow, more smirk than smile. Turned his head toward Eira, eyes glinting, taking his sweet time about it.","Eira knew right away he’d heard everything.","Not just heard it, either. Looked completely fine with where Claire’s little joke was headed. Looked like he was enjoying it.","She looked away fast, refused to meet his eyes.","Alpha Killian wasn’t in any rush to let her off the hook. Leaned in slow, elbow on the table, close enough that his voice dropped low, meant for her ears only.","\"So,\" he drawled, gaze steady on her, not blinking, not backing off an inch.","\"You figure out how you’re paying me back yet?\" A pause, corner of his mouth twitching up. \"Take your time. I’m not going anywhere.\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109 The Handoff","paragraphs":["Eira took a sip of her juice. \"Dinner. My treat.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes stayed locked on her. \"And?\"","She hesitated.","Couldn’t really pull the same card three times in a row. That’d just look lame.","No backup plan. No clever comeback loaded up and ready to fire.","So she flipped it back on him. \"What do you want, then?\"","Alpha Killian looked away, voice flat, case closed. \"I’ll let you know.\"","Eira let it drop. Went back to eating, watched him grab his glass and make the rounds. Toasted Beatrice. Toasted the Davies couple. Toasted Claire.","Same line, every single time. Short. No frills.","\"To you.\"","That’s all he said.","Didn’t match the guy everybody talked about behind his back. Cold. Ruthless.","The kind of Alpha who never wasted breath on small talk, who looked at a room full of people and picked out the weak link before anybody’d even shaken his hand. Rumor had it he’d once stared down a rival pack’s Alpha at a business dinner without blinking once, didn’t say a word, just let the guy sweat through his suit.","Then again, his mom was Seraphina Sterling. The kind of woman who lit up a room and made you feel like the only person in the world when she talked to you.","Made a little more sense, seeing it that way.","--","Dinner wrapped up fast after that.","Claire and Martin cleared plates, stacking them with a soft clatter. Davies rolled his sleeves up past his forearms, grabbed a dish rag off the counter like he’d done it a hundred times in this exact kitchen.","\"You don’t need to do that,\" Eira said, reaching to take the rag from him.","\"Dishwasher,\" Alpha Killian cut in, right on her heels, not even looking up from where he stood by the counter.","Too in sync. Like they’d planned it.","Davies froze mid-reach, rag still dangling from his fingers. He glanced over at the sleek built-in unit tucked under the counter, brand new, still had a faint smell of fresh plastic and metal.","\"Huh.\" He set the rag down slow, wiped his hands on his jeans instead. Raised an eyebrow at Eira. \"You bought that yourself?\"","\"Actually, Mr. Sterling did.\"","\"Mr. Sterling?\" Davies went quiet for a second. His gaze bounced between the two of them, lingered a beat too long. Then he just smiled, shook his head, and let it go.","Everyone cleared out fast after that. Martin and Davies went to grab the cars.","Eira walked Beatrice out first.","\"Text me when you’re home,\" Eira said.","Beatrice squeezed her hand, eyes glassy again, something unsaid sitting right behind them.","She didn’t say it, not with Alpha Killian standing right there, but Eira didn’t need the words spelled out. She could read it plain enough off Beatrice’s face.","[The Sovereign Processor Initiative’s finally going public tomorrow. Everything Alaric spent his life working toward.]","Eira’s throat went tight. \"I know.\"","Martin called from the driver’s seat. \"Bag in the back, for tomorrow. Don’t forget it.\"","\"Thanks, Martin.\"","Car pulled away.","Davies’s wife hugged Eira next, quick and warm. \"This place just went up in value, you know that?\"","\"What?\"","\"Tech world’s about to know your name. This house? Gonna be a landmark.\" She winked, climbed in.","Claire hung out the back window, waving both arms. \"See you tomorrow, Eira!\"","\"See you tomorrow.\"","Both cars turned the corner and were gone.","Eira turned back around. Alpha Killian was still standing there.","\"I’ll walk you to your car.\"","\"Too cold.\"","Not pride. Just fact.","His car rolled up seconds later. Driver hopped out, nodded. \"Miss Crawford.\" Opened the door.","Alpha Killian got in, then paused halfway, one hand on the doorframe. Glanced back at her, a lazy kind of smile tugging at his mouth.","\"So,\" he said. \"Still owe me for a couple things. You thought about that at all, or you just hoping I forget?\"","Eira crossed her arms. \"I don’t forget my debts. I just haven’t figured out what you’re worth yet.\"","\"Careful.\" He slid into the seat, one leg still out the door. \"Keep talking like that and I might start charging interest.\"","\"You wouldn’t.\"","\"Try me.\"","The door shut. Window rolled down halfway, just enough for his voice to carry.","\"Get some sleep, Crawford. Big day tomorrow.\" A beat. \"I’ll figure out what I want eventually. No rush.\"","Window rolled up. Car pulled off, taillights shrinking into the dark.","Eira stood there a second longer than she meant to, arms still crossed, trying to figure out if she’d just gotten teased or threatened. Probably both.","Back inside, Eira locked the door, dropped onto the couch, opened the bag Martin left. Typical Martin.","Guy had spent a whole week trying to drag her to salons and haul tailors to the house. Even lined up a few models built just like her so she could point and pick without trying anything on herself.","She shot him down every time. Never stopped him from stocking her closet anyway.","Grabbed the bag, headed upstairs. Quick shower, brushed her teeth, killed the lights.","Lay down, closed her eyes. Tomorrow was already on its way.","--","Dawn crept in pale and cold.","Alpha Sebastian was already up. Showered, standing in front of his closet, scanning the row of suits and ties.","Something felt off. The clothes weren’t packed as tight as usual. Extra space between the hangers. More room than there should’ve been.","He frowned, walked over to the other side of the closet. That’s where Eira used to keep her things.","Knock knock.","\"Alpha Sebastian, breakfast’s ready.\" The housekeeper’s voice from the hallway.","His father had insisted she stay the night. Didn’t trust restaurant food on the morning of a major bid. Wanted everything controlled. Clean.","\"Be right there.\"","Alpha Sebastian grabbed a tie, knotted it without even looking, headed downstairs.","The table was loaded. Eggs, bacon, pancakes, fresh fruit, a whole spread like she’d cooked for ten people instead of one. He sat down, picked at a few bites, barely tasted any of it.","He’d gotten used to Eira’s cooking. Her timing. The way she remembered exactly how he liked his coffee. Without that, nothing felt right.","The housekeeper hovered nearby, anxious. \"Something wrong, Alpha Sebastian? I can whip up something else.\"","\"It’s fine. Not your fault.\" He stood, grabbed his jacket. \"Just used to what my Luna made, that’s all.\"","Left before she could say anything back.","His assistant was waiting in the lobby when he pulled up.","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Why are you down here?\"","\"Finn Carter’s upstairs. In your office.\"","Alpha Sebastian stopped mid-step, turned around.","Finn Carter. Twenty-three. Alpha Carter’s youngest. The Alpha heir.","Golden boy showing up unannounced on bid day meant one of two things. Either nobody upstairs trusted Alpha Sebastian to close this deal, or a handoff was already in motion. Neither one sat well.","\"He say why he’s here?\"","\"No, Alpha Sebastian.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"It’s fine.\"","He pushed open his office door. Finn sat in his chair, grinning like he already owned the place.","\"Sebastian! Been a while, man.\"","\"Finn.\"","Finn stood up, casual in a hoodie and jeans, hands stuffed in his pockets. Looked like he’d rolled out of bed twenty minutes ago.","\"Dad said you’ve got a big one today. Told me to shadow you. Learn the ropes. You know how it is.\"","Alpha Sebastian caught that word right away.","Shadow.","Not \"help.\" Not \"observe.\" Shadow.","He kept his face neutral, stuck a hand out. \"Welcome aboard.\"","Finn’s handshake was firm, confident. He checked his watch. \"So when do we head out?\"","Alpha Sebastian smiled, smooth and controlled.","\"Right now.\""]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110 The Long Road","paragraphs":["At Sterling Group, Miles pushed open the office door.","Alpha Killian was already at his desk, signing off on the last of the day’s paperwork. Eight sharp.","\"Alpha Killian, R&D’s downstairs.\"","Alpha Killian capped his pen, looked up. \"Ten minutes. That’s it.\"","Meeting ran fast and tight. Ten minutes later, Alpha Killian stood. \"Half hour for breakfast. West entrance, eight-fifty.\"","Team cleared out. Alpha Killian turned to Miles. \"You got what I asked for?\"","Miles patted his briefcase. \"Right here.\"","\"Twenty copies. Get them into binders.\"","Alpha Killian’s voice stayed flat, but something sharp flickered behind his eyes.","Miles bolted for the copy room, roped in Natalie and Kate to help since the stack was massive.","Kate flipped through the first page, whistled low. \"He planning to hand these out like flyers or what?\"","Miles just smiled.","Couldn’t picture the scene exactly either, but he could picture the look on Alpha Killian’s face when he slid this thing across the table in front of the committee. Dead calm. Ice cold.","The kind of look that screamed game over before the other guy even knew he’d lost.","Natalie slid pages into binder covers, muttering. \"Karma’s a bitch. Dude’s about to get destroyed by the woman he tossed aside like garbage.\"","\"We seriously can’t tag along?\" Kate whined.","\"Nope. Somebody’s gotta hold the fort.\" Miles shrugged. \"You’ll hear all about it later, promise.\"","Kate huffed, slammed her stapler down. Caught herself. \"Careful. This paperwork’s about to tank our biggest competitor.\"","\"I know.\" Natalie glanced toward the hallway. \"Eira know about any of this?\"","\"Beats me.\" Kate shrugged.","Both of them went quiet a beat, a little wistful.","Miles cleared his throat. \"She knows. Hey, quit moping, you two. It’s not like she fell off the face of the earth. You’ll see her around.\"","He packed the twenty binders into a spare banker’s box from the supply closet, snapped the lid shut.","By eight-fifty, Alpha Killian’s car rolled out from Sterling Tower’s west entrance.","Twenty minutes later, they pulled up outside the downtown convention center, where the selection committee had a conference room booked for the day.","--","Southridge Estates, Number Nine.","Eira washed up, did her makeup light, popped in the colored contacts, prescription ones, exactly her strength. Martin thought of everything.","The outfit fit like it was made for her. Probably was. Black turtleneck, brown leather skirt, ankle boots she could actually walk in. She snapped a photo, sent it to Martin.","Martin: Coat. It’s sunny but freezing.","She grabbed the brown blazer off the bed and headed out.","A black sedan sat waiting at the gate.","Thomas Green behind the wheel, same driver who’d shuttled her between Sterling Group and the institute for four years. Except today he wasn’t alone. Two bodyguards in the back, boxing her in on both sides.","\"Morning, Dr. Crawford. Breakfast at the institute, or grab something on the road?\" Thomas caught her eye in the rearview. \"I’d say on the road. Random’s safer.\"","She hadn’t eaten. Hadn’t slept much either, too busy running through today in her head. \"On the road. Four meals, one for everybody.\"","He pulled over halfway, came back with breakfast sandwiches.","\"Expense it, Thomas.\"","\"Four years, Dr. Crawford. You’ve said that every single time.\" He grinned. \"I know.\"","She smiled, unwrapped her sandwich as the car rolled toward the convention center downtown.","Nine o’clock sharp, they pulled up.","--","Eira stepped out of the car, took the escalator upstairs, and headed for the institute team.","The room was already half full. Handshakes, nods, coffee cups.","Dr. Victor Winthrop broke away from a conversation and crossed over to her himself.","\"Dr. Crawford.\" He offered his hand. \"Long road. You made it count.\"","\"Thank you, Dr. Victor Winthrop.\" She shook it, polite, professional. \"I’m not on the panel, so I’ll be next door.\"","Davies walked her out. Lowered his voice once they hit the hallway.","\"One thing before you go. Both bidders are personal to you, one way or another. Sterling signed your paychecks, and Hale—\" he didn’t finish that one.","\"Point is, the panel knows it, and they’ll be watching for it. Whatever input you give at the end, make sure it’s bulletproof. Numbers, not feelings.\"","\"It will be.\"","\"I know.\" He paused, then added, simpler, \"Dr. Alaric would’ve liked seeing this. That’s all.\"","She nodded once and pushed into the small conference room.","\"There she is!\" Claire spun her chair around. The rest of the team looked up from their laptops, grinning.","\"So what’s the mood over there?\" someone called out. \"They look nervous? Tell me Hale looks nervous.\"","\"They look caffeinated.\" Eira dropped into a chair. \"Speaking of which, anyone order food? No? Okay, hands up, who hasn’t eaten.\"","Half the room, of course. She reached for her phone to put in an order.","Not there.","She checked her blazer, ran it back fast. Pocket at home, straight into the car. Backseat, had to be.","And her notes for the final Q&A were on it, no way she was walking into this afternoon without them.","\"Claire, call Thomas, tell him to swing back. I’ll run down and grab it.\" She was already up. Honestly, five minutes away from all this nervous energy didn’t sound bad either.","The bodyguards fell in behind her.","Down in the lobby, she clocked Serena camped on a couch by the entrance, head down, earbuds in, thumbs flying.","Texting Sebastian, probably.","Eira breezed right past. The bodyguards screened her from view, and Serena never looked up.","Thomas’s car was idling out front. He started to get out and help, but Eira waved him off.","\"I’ve got it.\" She leaned into the backseat, felt around, and there it was, wedged under the seat.","Right then a sleek Bentley rolled up behind the sedan.","She didn’t clock it at first. Then she caught the plate.","Alpha Sebastian’s car. New one, replacing the one Alpha Killian totaled.","Of course. Great timing.","She straightened up, phone in hand, as Alpha Sebastian stepped out. Tailored suit, polished shoes, assistant at his elbow. And a young guy she’d never seen before.","Alpha Sebastian didn’t notice her. His eyes were on the building.","But the young guy’s gaze had already found her. And stayed there.","\"Finn?\" Alpha Sebastian glanced over.","Finn’s eyes were wide, bright, a little glazed over.","Alpha Sebastian knew that dumbstruck look, he’d worn it himself once. Love at first sight. Who the hell is he...","He followed Finn’s gaze. And froze.","Eira. Except nothing like the Eira he knew. Sharp lines, put together, all confidence.","She met his stare dead-on. Colder than ever.","Why was she here, dressed like that? She’d quit Sterling.","Before he got a word out, Finn was already moving.","\"Give me a sec, Sebastian.\" He made a beeline for her, cheeks pink.","A bodyguard stepped into his path, arm out.","Finn clocked the security, did the math, somebody important, and grinned anyway. \"You here for the bid too? Finn Carter. What’s your name?\"","She sized him up. Couldn’t read his angle. \"Eira.\"","God, she’s so cool. \"Can I get your number?\"","\"Finn.\" Alpha Sebastian cut in, smile stretched thin, nowhere near his eyes. \"Eira. What are you doing here? And who are they?\"","Finn blinked between them. \"Wait, you two know each other?\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded, mouth already opening, she’s my wife locked and loaded.","\"Sebastian!\" Serena, at the entrance.","She stepped out and froze at the sight of them standing together. [Why the hell did he bring her here?]"]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111 You’re in My Seat","paragraphs":["Serena slid up next to Alpha Sebastian.","Finn caught Eira’s glance flick over the two of them. \"Who’s this?\"","\"A friend of Sebastian’s?\" Serena turned on the warmth, hand out. \"Serena Winthrop.\"","Finn left the hand hanging. Sure, he called Alpha Sebastian \"bro,\" didn’t make them buddies.","And his gut said Eira couldn’t stand this woman. He was still angling for points with Eira.","Alpha Sebastian’s brow twitched. He kept it flat. \"This is Finn Carter.\"","Couldn’t call him a friend. Couldn’t not. Keep it simple, Serena would connect the dots.","She did. Her smile slipped. Finn Carter. Alpha heir to Carter Pack.","\"Mr. Carter, I’m sorry, I didn’t realize...\"","Finn gave her a tight little smile, eyes already drifting back to Eira. The second she turned to leave, he was moving.","\"You heading in? I’ll walk with you!\"","\"Eira, where are you going?\" Alpha Sebastian stepped after her and walked straight into a bodyguard’s arm.","She glanced back. \"I have business here.\"","\"What business could you possibly have here?\" His voice sharpened. \"And who are these guys? Who put security on you?\"","[So she’s not here with Sebastian.] Serena’s confusion cleared. [If not him, that left exactly one possibility.]","Alpha Sebastian got there too. His jaw went tight. \"Sterling.\"","Serena’s lips curved. Of course. Running right back to Alpha Killian Sterling.","\"That would be me.\"","The voice came from behind them, low and even.","Eira looked up.","The Sterling delegation had rolled up at some point, Alpha Killian front and center, his team fanned out around him.","His gaze swept the group, stopped a beat on Finn. \"Mr. Carter. Been a while.\"","Finn grinned. \"Mr. Sterling. Good to see you.\"","\"Mm.\" That was all Finn got.","Alpha Killian’s eyes moved to Eira, boxed in on the sidewalk, and his chin tipped toward the doors. \"Go inside.\"","An exit. She took it, guards falling in beside her, Alpha Killian a step behind.","Alpha Sebastian moved to follow and somehow there was always a Sterling employee in his way. Casual about it. Airtight.","His fists clenched. [She takes orders from Sterling now? Does she even remember who her husband is?]","\"Sebastian.\" Serena reached for his fist. He pulled it away.","She froze. \"Sebastian?\"","He forced his face back to soft. \"Head on up. People might see.\"","She bit the inside of her cheek. \"Fine.\" Then, sweeter: \"See you up there, Mr. Carter.\"","Finn, who’d been doing his best impression of furniture: \"You coming, Sebastian?\"","\"Yeah.\"","By the elevators, Alpha Killian’s voice dropped. \"You used me again.\"","Eira’s head turned slow. Blank stare. What?","Behind them Miles kept his face professionally empty. [Alpha. You walked over there yourself. On purpose.]","The elevator dinged, too small for the whole crowd, and she had zero interest in sharing air with him anyway. She peeled off to the second car.","Doors slid shut. Alpha Killian replayed that wide-eyed blink, like a startled cat.","The corner of his mouth lifted.","--","The conference room buzzed with conversation. Serena scanned the room. No sign of Dr. Crawford.","\"Where’s Dr. Crawford?\"","Claire shrugged. \"Beats me.\"","Serena picked a seat and made herself comfortable. The long table had two power seats, one at the screen end, one right where she’d just planted her flag.","A researcher leaned over. \"Miss Winthrop, that’s Dr. Crawford’s seat.\"","The team had never warmed up to her. Right back at them, as far as she was concerned. She flashed a breezy smile. \"Well, she’s not here, is she? And rolling in late on the biggest day of the project? Not exactly lead-engineer material.\"","Claire sat up. \"She was here before you. She stepped out for a minute.\"","Serena just smiled. [ Naturally. President of the Dr. Crawford fan club, first to the rescue.]","On the big monitor, the main room was filling up. Committee taking their seats, corporate reps filing in, nameplates lined up down the table.","Sterling Group’s sat right next to Hale Group’s.","Alpha Killian took his seat, and his gaze slid to the one empty chair at the Hale nameplate. Something like amusement crossed his face.","[The Carter kid’s in the building. So who gets the chair?]","By title, it was Alpha Sebastian’s. He was the project lead. But with Carter money riding on Hale’s bid, he wasn’t touching that seat until Finn said so.","Dr. Victor Winthrop glanced at the empty spot. \"Is Hale Group’s representative not joining us?\"","\"I’m here.\" Alpha Sebastian gave a polite nod. He knew the face; Serena had shown him photos.","Finn waved a lazy hand. \"Go ahead, Sebastian.\"","Only then did Alpha Sebastian sit.","Dr. Victor Winthrop sized him up. Heard plenty about this kid, never met him in the flesh.","[Composed. Hungry. Parked next to Killian Sterling and not even sweating. No wonder Serena was head over heels.","Kid like that, with the right people behind him, goes places. And the two Packs joining up? Win-win all around.]","He gave a satisfied little nod and leaned toward a colleague. \"Keep tabs on Hale Group.\"","Nobody needed subtitles. The old man was betting on Hale.","--","Five to ten. Main room went church-quiet. Small room was buzzing.","Claire kept eyeballing the door. [Come on, where are you?]","Serena watched the same door, running very different math. [If Dr. Crawford flakes, today might just fall right into my lap.]","The door opened.","Eira walked in, security in tow.","Every head snapped around.","Serena’s sneer fired on pure reflex. \"Eira, sweetie, wrong room. Plus-ones wait in the lounge. This one’s team only.\"","Eira kept coming, no rush, every step landing right where she wanted it.","She stopped square in front of Serena. Her eyes flicked down to her face. Then to the chair under her.","\"Miss Winthrop,\" she said, quiet as anything. \"You’re in my seat.\""]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112 One More Thing","paragraphs":["Serena felt like she’d just heard the punchline to the world’s meanest joke.","She stayed planted, chin up, looking Eira over like something stuck to her shoe. \"Cute outfit. But playing dress-up doesn’t make you somebody, Eira. You share a name with Dr. Crawford, that’s it. Don’t start believing your own fairy tale.\"","Eira glanced at the two men by the door.","That was all it took. Both bodyguards lifted Serena clean out of the chair in front of the whole room. She twisted against their grip and got nowhere.","\"What the hell!\"","Claire was already rolling a fresh chair into the gap, bright as sunshine. \"Morning, Dr. Crawford.\"","Serena’s head whipped around.","The rest of the team looked up from their laptops and echoed it, easy and automatic, the way people greet someone they’ve greeted a thousand mornings running. \"Morning, Dr. Crawford.\"","Eira sat. \"Breakfast’s on the way up. Grab what you can, we’ll do a real break at lunch.\" Then she lifted her eyes to Serena’s blank stare, cool as you like. \"Miss Winthrop. Maybe you’re the one who should quit fooling herself.\"","On the wall monitor, the live feed from the main conference room was already running, the first bidder setting up at the podium. Eira nodded at an empty chair. \"Sit.\"","Serena couldn’t move. She’d heard the name Eira Crawford before and wondered, sure. Same city, same name, what were the odds?","But the Eira she knew did Alpha Sebastian’s laundry, and the Hales had always sold her as some forty-grand-a-year admin who’d been Alpha Killian Sterling’s secretary for a hot minute. That woman running the Sovereign Processor Initiative?","Either this whole room was in on a prank, or Serena had been catastrophically wrong.","Breakfast arrived, a box for everyone. Even her.","She stared at the steaming coffee, chest heaving. \"What proof do you have that you’re Dr. Crawford?\"","\"I’m sitting in this seat. That’s your proof.\"","A researcher jumped in. \"We’ve worked with her for years, Miss Winthrop. You joined at the tail end, makes sense you never crossed paths.\"","Claire piled on, sweet as pie. \"She can always ask Dr. Victor Winthrop. He’s called Dr. Crawford into his office plenty of times.\"","Everyone knew what those meetings had been about. Her.","Serena’s jaw locked. She spun for the door. She needed to hear it from her grandfather.","\"Miss Winthrop. Where do you think you’re going?\"","One look from Eira and the guards were at the exit.","\"Session’s live. Nobody leaves, standard leak protocol.\" A slight tilt of the head. \"Sit down on your own, or should I have someone help you?\"","The guards rolled their shoulders.","No play left.","Serena stalked back and slammed the bag on the table. Loud. Petty. All she had.","Eira didn’t look up. \"Keep it down.\"","Serena’s knuckles went white around the strap.","--","The room was locked in on the presentations, company after company taking the floor for the Sovereign Processor.","Serena sat drowning in her own head.","[If Sebastian finds out how brilliant she is, does he ever let her go? What if the Hales flip overnight? ]","And the contract signing this afternoon.","She was supposed to be by Alpha Sebastian’s side.","She glanced at the guards by the door and felt her stomach drop. She wasn’t getting anywhere near that room today.","On screen, Alpha Sebastian pitched to the committee, smooth as ever.","She felt zero pride. Her grandfather praised Hale’s proposal and all it did was scare her.","Claire leaned over. \"Dr. Crawford, so far Hale’s design lines up best with our specs.\"","\"Let’s hear the rest.\" Eira glanced at the screen. The main room had gone to recess. \"Take five, everybody. Hydrate.\"","Serena shot up and went for the door.","The guards didn’t blink.","\"What is your problem?\" She spun on Eira.","Eira looked honestly puzzled. \"Did Dr. Victor Winthrop not walk you through protocol? Nobody leaves, nobody contacts the outside. Breaks included.\"","\"It was all in the briefing packet,\" Claire chimed in, helpful as ever. \"Did you not read it?\"","Serena went red to the ears. \"Why didn’t you tell Sebastian who you are?\"","Eira leaned against the table, steam curling off her coffee, tone almost entertained. \"Everyone on this program signed the same NDA. Nothing leaves these walls without written clearance.\"","Her gaze sharpened. \"And clearance comes from one person. Me. Every disclosure gets logged with my signature on it.\"","A beat. \"You came in at the tail end, Miss Winthrop, but you know what a classified federal program is. And you know exactly what it means to feed pieces of one to a company that’s bidding on it.\"","The implication landed.","Serena’d been performing for the Hales the whole time, dropping hints to make herself seem indispensable. Right in front of Eira.","The thought hit like glass sliding down her throat.","Eira let the silence stretch.","[She’d had the authority from day one. One signature on a clearance form, and Sebastian could have walked into that room ahead of every Alpha in the country.","She’d almost filed it once. Black folder tucked against her chest. Twenty feet from the conference room before she’d turned around.","Best decision she’d ever made.]","\"Leave Sebastian out of this,\" she managed. \"Whatever happens, remember what you two had. Don’t do anything reckless.\"","Eira almost laughed.","[Her whole world cracking, and Serena was worried about him.","True love. Adorable.]","She didn’t dignify it with an answer. Just picked up her pen and went back to her notes, like Serena had already left the room.","Break was almost up.","Serena took one last shot. \"Think it through, Eira. If Sebastian loses this bid, what do you actually get?\"","\"Whoever wins, I get paid.\" Eira didn’t look up. \"The core architecture is patented in my name. The government licenses it, the winning bidder licenses it from the government, and the majority share of that pool routes back to me. Anybody ships a single unit, somebody’s writing me a check.\"","Serena’s breath caught. Hale wins, Hale writes those checks. Sterling wins, Sterling does. Either way it lands in Eira’s account.","And the marriage math was worse: Alpha Sebastian was the one who’d cheated. If Eira filed, she’d take him apart in court and enjoy it. If Eira just never files, Serena stays the other woman forever. Her family would disown her first.","The walls were closing in.","\"So you’ve known all along. About us.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"About what, exactly?\"","No answer. Some words you can’t say out loud."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113 The Fifteenth of the Month","paragraphs":["The presentations rolled on. Serena sat rigid in her chair, mind spinning through exits.","There weren’t any.","The clock ran down. Sterling Group had drawn the final slot.","Alpha Killian took his place beside the screen. Low, steady voice, no wasted words, laying out how Sterling would put the Sovereign Processor into power grids, border defense systems, and remote territories still running on hardware nobody in this country builds.","A big swing. But with Sterling’s money and Sterling’s connections, nobody in the room doubted they could land it.","He closed strong.","\"The Sovereign Processor is a step toward real independence. Our grids, our border systems, our territories, all of it running on chips we buy from somewhere else. We’ve been leasing the brains of our own infrastructure long enough. Sterling is committed to making sure this one stays in our hands.\"","Eira allowed herself the smallest smile. He’d nailed it. Tied the whole pitch back to what this project was built for in the first place: security and self-reliance.","Her team clapped along.","Claire leaned over. \"This one’s gonna be close. Hale’s got the industry track record, Sterling’s got the resources and the vision. Coin flip.\"","People started gathering their things.","Then Alpha Killian spoke again.","\"One more thing. I have a document for the committee.\"","He glanced at Miles.","Miles popped the lid off the box and started working his way down the table, laying a bound copy in front of each committee member.","The room went dead quiet.","--","\"What’s in it?\" Claire squinted at the feed.","Eira didn’t open her copy. She already knew.","In the main hall, nobody was packing up anymore. Reps from every bidding company dropped back into their chairs. Somebody near the door said, \"Hell of a time for an encore.\"","Alpha Sebastian didn’t laugh.","Something felt off. Alpha Killian Sterling didn’t do surprises. He did setups, and he did them early, and by the time you noticed one you were already standing in it.","Miles worked down the committee side of the table. Twenty seats, twenty folders. Then the box was empty. The company reps got nothing.","Covers opened. Pages turned.","Then the room went quiet, all at once, the way it does when twenty people hit the same line together.","Every head turned toward Victor Winthrop.","Victor hadn’t touched his. He opened it.","Page one stopped him cold.","Page two made him shut the folder and shove it away like it was hot.","\"Mr. Sterling. What is this?\"","Alpha Killian hadn’t left the podium. He sounded like a man reading a delivery schedule.","\"Sterling ran diligence on the consultant roster last month. We found something. Our counsel says we’re required to report it, so I’m reporting it. That’s all this is.\"","\"Where did you get any of this?\" Victor’s voice cracked on it. \"You don’t have access to private accounts.\"","\"We don’t, and we didn’t.\" Alpha Killian turned to the first tab. \"Everything in section one is public. Deed of sale. Vehicle title. Two LLC filings. My team pulled it in an afternoon.\"","He turned to the second tab.","\"Section two is a sworn declaration from Hale Group’s former assistant controller. She flagged the same payment eleven times and got moved to a different department for it. She signed that in front of our counsel last Thursday and she’s willing to sign it again for you.\"","\"Get to it,\" an official said.","\"Serena Winthrop is an external consultant on this program.\" He didn’t look at a single note. \"The fifteenth of every month, Hale Group wires her three hundred thousand dollars. Same day, same amount, same account. Forty-eight months running. Their books call it research funding.\"","A pause.","\"Fourteen point four million.\"","The room came apart. Not loud. Worse. Twenty people talking low and fast at the same time, three laptops closing at once.","Alpha Sebastian shot to his feet.","Two rooms away, Serena did the same thing at the same second.","\"Sterling isn’t saying what that money was for,\" Alpha Killian said. \"I’ll say nobody funds research on the fifteenth of the month.\"","He turned a page.","\"And it didn’t come out of Mr. Hale’s pocket. It cleared through a Hale Group operating account, forty-eight times, coded to R&D. Somebody in that building approved every one of them.\"","Two of the committee members looked at each other.","\"Last eight months, Miss Winthrop bought a penthouse north of a million. Jewelry. A car titled to a Hale corporate account. Paperwork’s in the packet.\"","He turned to the committee.","\"We’re asking for a full audit of every transfer and every message between them. And we’re asking the record to show Sterling brought it.\"","Alpha Sebastian went white, then red. \"This is a hit job and you’re all just sitting here.\"","\"Mr. Hale.\" The chair didn’t look up. \"I’d stop talking.\"","\"You can’t let him stand there and—\"","\"Sit down. This session’s on the record.\"","Hale’s outside counsel leaned into Alpha Sebastian’s ear. Whatever he said, Alpha Sebastian sat.","Alpha Killian hadn’t moved once.","Alpha Sebastian might as well have been yelling at a parked car.","\"Dr. Victor Winthrop.\" The chair finally looked up. \"Who signed her conflict-of-interest form?\"","Victor’s face had gone blotchy red down into his collar. \"She was vetted. She signed the same NDA everybody signed. She would never put this program at risk.\"","\"That’s not what I asked. Who signed it?\"","Silence.","\"Doctor.\"","\"I did.\""]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114 Taken In","paragraphs":["\"Then explain the fifteenth of the month,\" another official said, flat. \"Not the total. The pattern. Because a bidder putting a government consultant on a monthly schedule isn’t funding. Forget how it looks. That’s a retainer.\"","\"They’re together.\" Victor’s jaw worked. \"They’re a couple. Gifts between partners are normal.\"","He heard how thin it sounded before he got to the end of it.","\"A couple.\" Alpha Killian let it sit for a beat. \"Strange words, Dr. Victor. Mr. Hale’s been married four years.\"","The room died.","Forty-eight months of wires. Forty-eight months of marriage.","Nobody at that table needed help lining up two numbers. Half of them stopped hearing an affair right there and started hearing a payroll.","Alpha Sebastian never said the wife’s name. Not once.","Behind the annex glass, Eira picked up her coffee. Cold an hour ago. She drank it anyway.","Serena turned around slowly. \"You knew.\"","\"I told you. Nothing leaves this program without my signature.\" Eira set the cup down and nodded at the screen. \"That didn’t come from me.\"","--","Victor stood so fast his chair barked on the floor. His hands were shaking. For a second it looked like his legs were done.","Messi hadn’t said ten words all day. Contracting officer. He closed his folder and set it down.","\"We’re done. Evaluation’s suspended. Hale Group is out pending review, and I’m calling the Inspector General from this room.\"","\"You can’t just—\" Alpha Sebastian started.","\"Already did.\" Messi looked up. \"Litigation hold, effective now. Nobody deletes anything. Email, texts, calendars, not a sticky note. That’s every company in this room.\"","He nodded at the security officer by the door.","\"And go get Miss Winthrop out of the annex. She doesn’t leave the building.\"","Nobody argued.","--","The feds showed up inside an hour.","Not city cops. Two cars from the Inspector General’s office and a third nobody could place. They came in through the loading dock so the lobby cameras wouldn’t pick anything up.","A woman in a navy blazer held up a badge at the front of the hall. \"Special Agent Reyes, Office of the Inspector General. Nobody leaves this floor without checking out with me.\"","Alpha Sebastian and Serena got walked out separately, one from each room. No cuffs. Reyes said \"voluntary interview\" twice, loud enough for everybody to hear, and everybody understood how voluntary it was.","Victor Winthrop went too. He cooperated. He also needed a hand getting to the elevator.","Nobody else said a word.","One morning. Alpha Killian walked up to a podium, read some numbers off a page, and let the government do the rest. No leak, no press, no raised voice. Hale was out.","Finn Carter looked like the floor had dropped. Ten minutes ago Hale was neck and neck with Sterling. Now Hale was a headline.","And he was supposed to be here learning from Alpha Sebastian.","Finn started dialing his father.","--","Three rooms on the fourth floor. Three very different conversations.","Room A.","Serena had her arms crossed and her chin up. No lawyer. She’d asked for her grandfather twice and gotten nothing.","\"What’s your relationship with Sebastian Hale?\"","\"We’re friends.\"","\"Friends.\" The agent didn’t look up. \"Friends who buy each other penthouses. Try again.\"","\"He’s generous. That’s not a crime.\"","\"Three hundred grand on the fifteenth, forty-eight months straight. That’s not generous, that’s payroll.\" Now he looked up. \"Generous is a birthday.\"","\"I didn’t leak anything.\" Her voice climbed. \"I don’t even have access to the core data. Eira Crawford locked me out of the main lab day one. Go ask her. Ask anybody on that floor.\"","He wrote something down.","\"So you took fourteen million from a bidder and gave him nothing back.\"","Serena opened her mouth.","Nothing came out.","Room B.","Same opener, different chair.","\"What’s your relationship with Serena Winthrop?\"","Hale’s counsel was right beside him. \"You don’t have to answer.\"","\"Friends. And she didn’t leak anything. I didn’t need her to. My people built that proposal from scratch.\"","\"Generous friend.\" The agent flipped a page. \"She’s in a penthouse downtown. You’re in a three bedroom on Ashford. Interesting priorities.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","\"Say that again. Ashford’s still in my name?\"","\"Should it be in somebody else’s?\"","He didn’t answer.","He’d signed that transfer himself. Weeks ago. A title change takes four weeks, six if the county’s dragging.","So she’d walked out with the keys and never filed it.","She hadn’t wanted the house.","\"Mr. Hale.\" The agent tapped the table. \"Are you and Miss Winthrop romantically involved?\"","His lawyer’s hand came down flat. \"Don’t.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at the table. The silence answered for him.","\"That’s got nothing to do with a leak.\"","\"Answer the question.\"","He nodded.","\"Out loud, please. We’re recording.\"","\"Yes.\"","The agent wrote it down and took his time doing it. Then he turned the page, and something in his face shifted. Not harder. Almost curious.","\"Last question for now, Mr. Hale. What does your wife do for a living?\"","The question landed wrong.","Alpha Sebastian turned it over and it still didn’t fit. Who else would Eira be?","Whatever showed on his face, the agent across the table caught it. He didn’t push. He made a note, the second agent made one too, and they left it sitting there like something they’d come back to.","\"What’s that supposed to mean?\"","\"We ask, you answer, Mr. Hale.\" The agent turned a page. \"Every contact you’ve had with Serena Winthrop. Start at the beginning.\"","\"Serena never gave me anything classified.\"","That part he wasn’t sweating. Every time she tried to slide him lab data he shut it down. Half to keep her clean, half to keep himself clean.","Sterling was the part he never saw coming. The Alpha had built a file on him and dropped it in the middle of a federal bid. No warning shot. Just the hit, timed for the week it would cost the most.","He’d take it to Eira, too. Of course he would.","The research money Alpha Sebastian could still call an investment. The condo, the bracelet, the car in her garage titled in his name? Good luck.","And if a reporter got a shot of him walking out with an agent’s hand on his elbow, he was finished by the morning news.","Alpha Sebastian could bury that much. His PR team was the best money could buy, and they’d killed uglier stories than this one. Two calls, a friendly editor, and by Thursday nobody would remember.","But Finn Carter was the part nobody could bury.","The Carter pack held enough Hale Group stock to come with a board seat, and Finn hadn’t heard about this secondhand. He’d stood in that room and watched it happen. Nothing to deny, nobody to sue.","He wouldn’t even have to play dirty. Let the story run, let the stock bleed, call an emergency board meeting and ask one question: who lost us the contract. Pick up whatever shares came loose while people were scared, then go after Alpha Sebastian’s seat with the room already on his side.","Nobody was taking that hit for him."]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115 Taken Down","paragraphs":["Down the hall, Serena had stopped pretending to cooperate.","\"You can stop looking at me like that. I’m not the other woman here. Eira is.\"","\"Miss Winthrop, I’ll say this one more time. You’re entitled to have an attorney present.\"","\"I don’t need one, because I haven’t done anything.\" She pushed her cup a few inches away. \"Sebastian and I were together first. She came along when he was at rock bottom and she got her hooks in and she made sure it stuck. He doesn’t love her. He has never loved her. So yes, he bought me things. What part of that is confusing to you?\"","The agent wrote something down.","\"He married her because the timing worked. He picked me. You tell me which one of us is the mistress.\"","\"Noted. Back to the question.\"","\"I never told him anything classified and he never asked me to. I couldn’t have anyway. Eira Crawford had me locked out of the main lab inside a week, ask anybody, ask her, she’ll tell you herself. She wouldn’t let me near a terminal.\"","\"Sit back, please.\"","\"This is unbelievable.\"","\"Sit back, Miss Winthrop. Now tell me about the car.\"","Two doors down, Dr. Victor Winthrop had a paper cup of water in front of him and a lawyer at his shoulder, and he’d given the same three answers a dozen different ways without once raising his voice.","He had no knowledge of any financial arrangement involving his granddaughter. She had never held core access, so there was nothing available for her to disclose.","Her placement had gone through the ordinary channels, which he would encourage them to review.","An hour of it. Then they sent in somebody else.","The new one didn’t warm up. He put two folders on the table, Serena’s personnel file and the original hiring requirements for the Sovereign Processor Initiative, and he left them both closed.","\"Her paperwork’s in order. It’s the timing I keep coming back to.\"","\"The program encountered a technical issue. We retained an outside consultant with overseas training. I’d refer you to the protocol on consultant hires, it’s not a determination I made alone.\"","\"Dr. Crawford resolved that issue. Your granddaughter never touched it.\"","\"Dr. Crawford declines to work collaboratively with anyone. I’d hardly hold my granddaughter responsible for that.\"","The agent left the folders where they were.","\"She’s been on that project a few weeks. You can’t name me one thing she contributed and you can’t tell me why she needed to be in that building. That’s a problem for somebody. It might not be a problem for me.\"","Dr. Victor Winthrop’s lawyer leaned in and said something short.","\"Unless you have evidence my granddaughter disclosed classified material,\" Dr. Victor Winthrop said, \"I think we’re finished.\"","\"You are. She isn’t. Neither is Mr. Hale.\"","The lead agent motioned for someone to walk him out. He’d come in as a witness. He hadn’t touched a dollar of Alpha Sebastian Hale’s money and how Serena got hired was going to be somebody’s problem at the institute long before it was ever the Bureau’s, and everyone in the room understood that, which was most of why he’d been so calm.","He was through the door with his coat over his arm when the agent spoke again.","\"One more thing, Doctor.\"","He stopped.","\"The institute called about twenty minutes ago. Late hire, no contribution on record, open security review. Leadership took a vote. She’s off the Sovereign Processor Initiative as of this morning.\"","The color drained out of his face.","All of it for nothing. Every call he’d made, every marker he’d called in, every old colleague he’d leaned on until they stopped picking up.","He had spent down his own name to get Serena’s badge into that lab, and she’d been one breakthrough away from first author on the paper that mattered. The kind of credit that follows you the rest of your career.","Twenty minutes on the phone and it was gone.","His ears started ringing. The hallway tilted. He grabbed for the doorframe and missed.","Somebody yelled for a medic. Ten minutes later the sirens pulled out of the lot with him on a gurney.","--","Back at the convention center, lunch was almost over.","Davies found her in the hallway with a copy of Alpha Killian’s file in his hand. It had been balled up and flattened so many times the creases had gone soft.","\"You want to see this?\" He asked it like he was hoping she’d pass.","Claire took it right out of his hand.","Then she stopped.","\"This is where it all came from? The bags, the car, the condo? He was paying for every bit of it?\"","\"Yeah.\"","\"For how long?\"","\"Long enough.\"","Claire looked back down at the page and her hand started shaking. \"This says three hundred a month. Three hundred thousand. While you were on his insurance and driving a car with a hundred and forty thousand miles on it.\"","\"That sounds right.\"","\"I want to throw up.\"","Davies crouched, gathered the pages Claire had let slip, flipped through a few. He read enough to see why, then walked it over and dropped it in the trash.","\"Don’t sit here reading that.\"","Eira’s mouth twitched. \"I’m the one who gave Mr. Sterling that number. It’s why I filed for divorce.\"","She’d handed over the amount and the account it came out of. It had gone all the way around and come back to take Alpha Sebastian’s contract with it.","Davies didn’t answer. His hand closed tight on his bag strap.","Claire had plenty to say. She went for two straight minutes, mostly variations on garbage and a couple of things she’d never have said in front of Davies on a normal day. He let her finish.","Eira filled a cup and put it in her hand halfway through.","\"Hale Group’s out of the bid,\" Davies said when she ran out of air. \"And leadership voted on Serena this morning. She’s off the project. Her name won’t be on anything.\"","\"Shut up. Seriously?\"","Eira’s shoulders came down an inch.","\"What about the leak?\" Claire said. \"Did she actually do it?\"","Davies shook his head.","Two agents came up the hall before he could get into it.","\"Dr. Crawford. Couple of follow-ups.\"","\"Sure.\"","\"You never gave Miss Winthrop access to core data. That accurate?\"","Eira looked at the one asking, then at the one with the notebook. She knew exactly what this was. No access, no leak, nothing to see here.","\"That’s accurate. I never gave her access.\"","She let it sit a beat.","\"That doesn’t mean she never got near it. I have video of her in the main lab after hours, at a terminal that wasn’t hers, pulling at files she wasn’t cleared for.\""]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116 Pleasure Doing Business","paragraphs":["The agents left.","Eira went back to the team’s table. Lunch was on the same floor as the company reps and the room was packed.","Results at two. Everybody waiting.","Nobody was talking about the contract, though. They were talking about Alpha Sebastian Hale and Serena Winthrop.","A leak investigation was bad. A married CEO covering his girlfriend’s condo was worse. Half the room was already running the numbers.","The other half was running numbers on Alpha Killian Sterling.","He hadn’t said a word in public. He’d walked into a federal bid with a file and let it do the work.","When he came through the room the greetings started up on both sides, Mr. Sterling, Mr. Sterling, and there was something careful in every one of them.","He didn’t answer any of them. Then he saw Eira in the middle of the project team and slowed down.","Miles followed his boss’s eyes.","Miss Crawford wasn’t a guest here. She was seated with the team, and Miles knew the guy next to her from a gala last year. Whatever her title was, it wasn’t small.","So that explained the lobby this morning. Why Alpha Killian hadn’t pushed when she passed on the elevator.","\"Seats are up front, Alpha.\" Miles kept it quiet, and it meant something else.","Don’t stand here looking at her. There are forty phones in this room.","Alpha Killian turned and kept walking.","Eira glanced up and caught the side of his face going past.","Her phone buzzed.","Lila: Eira!!! Are you watching this? My brother’s bidding on Dr. Thorne’s chip project today. Whole family’s parked in front of the TV. I might throw up.","Lila: No clue if he’s got it. They announce this afternoon. Fingers crossed.","Lila: Also I still don’t know who took over the project after Dr. Thorne died and it is EATING ME ALIVE. Whoever it is has to be scary smart. Tried to pry it out of people at the gala and got nowhere. Not dropping it this time.","Eira: Saw it. And then what?","Four seconds later:","Lila: Then I track them down and make them build a custom chip for my robot. I’ll pay. I’ll beg. I have no shame.","Eira’s mouth twitched.","Eira: Busy for a bit. Talk later.","She pocketed the phone and finished eating.","At two, the press came in.","Reporters in the hall.","The Sterlings at home, watching for Alpha Killian’s face on the feed. The Hales, watching for Alpha Sebastian and Serena to walk into frame, because that would mean they’d won.","The broadcast ran on a delay. Nobody outside the building knew a thing yet.","Inside, the institute’s director stepped up to the mic.","\"Congratulations to Sterling Group.\"","The room let out one long breath.","You could hear it move. Every company that lost sat back at once, and then the looks started drifting toward the Sterling side of the room.","The Sterling engineers didn’t bother with dignity. Sterling Group’s R&D arm had been on this thing for two years and they were out of their chairs, hollering, grabbing each other by the shoulders.","Davies started clapping. The next table picked it up, then the next, and inside ten seconds the whole hall was going.","Alpha Killian never left his seat.","He gave the director a short nod, brought his hands up, and clapped. Unhurried. A man applauding somebody else’s news.","He found Eira without turning his head.","She looked up at the same time.","Her mouth lifted at the corner. [Congratulations.]","His eyebrow moved, barely. [You too.]","--","Signing at three, same hall. The institute wanted all the reps to stick around for it.","Alpha Killian sent Miles down the row. Ties, pens, right copy in the right folder, run the order one more time. Nothing sloppy.","Davies was doing the same thing on the other side of the room.","\"Signing’s quick, nobody asks you anything. Then they do the awards, federal commendations, bonus letters, same room while the press is still here. That’s where somebody tries for a personal question.\"","He looked at Eira.","\"You’re a federal honoree as of this afternoon. Nobody’s going to lean on you. Answer what you want, let the rest go.\"","Eira nodded. Then her lips pressed together. \"Where’s the water?\"","Davies grinned. \"Nervous?\"","\"A little.\"","\"I got you.\" Claire was already up.","Three cups later Eira had been to the restroom twice.","Coming out the second time she found Alpha Killian across the hall with his hands in his pockets. Everybody else was inside getting seated.","\"Mr. Sterling.\"","He looked at her a second, then pulled a tin out of his jacket.","She looked at it. Didn’t reach.","His jaw tightened.","\"It’s not poisoned.\"","A beat.","\"Helps you focus.\"","Obviously it wasn’t poisoned. She just didn’t see why the man who’d won the contract twenty minutes ago was standing in a hallway handing out Altoids.","Before she got her hand up he flipped the lid, put one in his own mouth, took out a second, and stepped in.","It stopped an inch from her lips.","\"Open.\"","Not a request.","Her mouth opened before she’d decided anything.","Cold hit the back of her nose and kept going.","He snapped the tin shut and walked off toward the hall.","Eira bit down on it. Her eyes watered.","[Okay. That worked.]","--","Stage lights, two rows of cameras, and a long table with a folder squared up at each end.","Alpha Killian Sterling and Eira Crawford sat down across from each other.","The institute’s contracting officer signed the first page of both copies and stepped back, and after that it was the two of them.","They signed their own copies, slid them across the table, and signed again. Someone off to the side checked both folders and gave the director a small nod.","They stood up.","Alpha Killian put his hand out first.","\"Pleasure doing business, Dr. Crawford.\"","She took it.","\"Likewise, Mr. Sterling.\""]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117 Everyone Was Watching","paragraphs":["The Sterling Manor.","The TV had been on for an hour and nobody was really watching it. Luna Seraphina had her feet up with a glass of wine. Lila was on the couch with her phone in one hand and a bowl of chips balanced on her knee.","Alpha Julian had come through twice, said he had calls, and both times ended up standing behind the couch instead.","Alpha Killian came up on screen.","Alpha Julian didn’t say anything. He just uncrossed his arms.","Luna Seraphina glanced back at him and let it go.","\"He looks tired,\" she said.","\"He’s fine.\"","\"I’m just saying he looks tired.\"","Even Lila, who fought with her brother recreationally, had to give him this one.","\"Okay. He’s kind of a badass. I’m saying it once and I’ll deny it.\"","Then the camera cut to the other side of the table.","Lila’s chips went everywhere.","\"WAIT.\"","\"Lila, the rug.\"","\"MOM. That’s Eira.\"","\"Who?\"","\"Eira. Eira.\" She was up off the couch and about two feet from the screen. \"That’s Killian’s assistant. That’s the girl. Dad, tell her.\"","Alpha Julian had seen a photo of her months back, right after Alpha Killian moved her into that job, because he’d wanted to know who his son had suddenly parked ten feet from his desk.","\"That’s her,\" he said.","Luna Seraphina put her wine down.","Lila had both hands in her hair. \"I have been trying to find out who runs that project for two years. Two years. I sat next to her at the Ashford thing. I asked her. I said, do you have any idea who’s actually leading it, and she said—\"","\"What did she say?\"","\"She said she’d ask around.\"","Luna Seraphina laughed so hard she had to put a hand over her mouth.","\"That’s not funny.\"","\"It’s a little funny, honey.\"","On screen the two of them turned toward the cameras and the shutters went off in a wall of white.","Alpha Julian whistled through his teeth.","\"The Hales had her in the house for four years and never bothered to find out what she did for a living.\"","\"And now she’s on our side of the table,\" Luna Seraphina said.","\"Now she’s on our side of the table.\"","\"That’s not the same as her being on his side of anything.\" She picked her wine back up. \"Twenty bucks he blows it inside a month.\"","Lila spun around. \"You’re betting against your own kid?\"","\"I’m being realistic.\" Luna Seraphina didn’t look away from the screen.","\"No, I’m in. I want in.\" Lila climbed back over the arm of the couch. \"Fifty. He’s going to say something insane to her and not understand why it landed wrong.\"","Alpha Julian looked at his wife. \"You’re his mother.\"","\"I’ve met him.\"","\"He came out of you.\"","\"And he still doesn’t call me back.\" Luna Seraphina didn’t even look over.","Lila pointed the remote at her father. \"Face it, Dad. Killian’s got two settings. Three words, or scorched earth.\"","\"A man in love finds the words,\" Alpha Julian said. \"It takes the edge off him.\"","The room went quiet.","Lila looked at her mother. Her mother looked back.","\"Did he just say that out loud?\"","\"He says things like that.\"","\"Where does he even get them?\"","\"That one’s how he got me,\" Luna Seraphina said, and drank her wine.","--","The Hale Estate","Alpha Roger had been in the chair since morning. He hadn’t eaten. He hadn’t taken a single call.","Luna Margaret and Isabella were having a great day.","They’d done face masks after breakfast. By lunch they’d moved on to which salon could fit them in and what they were wearing tonight.","If Alpha Sebastian brought home the federal contract, the Carters would throw the dinner, and everybody worth knowing would be there. You didn’t show up to that in whatever was hanging in the closet.","Twenty minutes before the broadcast, Alpha Roger looked over at them.","\"Sit down.\"","\"We’re coming, we’re coming.\"","Luna Margaret crossed the room and dropped onto the couch. Isabella came down next to her and leaned into her shoulder.","\"So did he get it? He got it, right? Serena’s on the team.\"","\"Of course he got it.\" Luna Margaret patted her knee. \"Serena’s on the team, her grandfather’s behind him, and your brother is very good at what he does. We’ll be at that dinner tonight. You watch.\"","Alpha Roger’s jaw moved. He let it go. There was no version of that conversation that ended before three in the morning.","\"Yes.\"","Isabella’s eyes lit up.","The last industry thing she’d gone to had been a waste of a dress. Engineers. A lot of men in their fifties talking about supply chains.","She had met Felix Shaw there. They’d traded numbers, and then he’d never texted her again. She’d tried twice. He answered both times, said almost nothing, and that was that. She stopped. There’s nothing sadder than a girl who keeps reaching.","And honestly, Felix wasn’t even that big a deal. His grandfather was famous if you cared about federal research programs, which nobody she knew did.","The Carters were something else.","Finn Carter would be there tonight. One year older than her. And Alpha Sebastian was practically family to them at this point, which put her about as close to the front of the line as a person could get.","If she handled it right.","\"What are you smiling about?\"","\"Nothing.\" Isabella grinned. \"Good things.\"","\"It’s on,\" Alpha Roger said.","All three of them turned toward the screen.","\"Today the Sovereign Processor Initiative held its contract award at the Federal Convention Center in Hall 22. The winning bidder is Sterling Group.\"","Nobody moved.","Luna Margaret’s smile stayed on her face about two seconds longer than it should have, then came off.","\"Wait.\" Isabella sat up. \"Sterling? No. It was supposed to be Alpha Sebastian.\"","\"It was supposed to be us.\" Luna Margaret’s voice climbed. \"Serena was in that building. Her grandfather was in that building. What happened?\"","Alpha Roger didn’t answer.","He’d spent all day bracing for a win he’d have to spend the next year defending. Losing hadn’t been on the list.","The feed cut to the hall. Reps filing in, cameras along the wall, the seal on the front of the table.","No Serena. No Dr. Winthrop. Nobody from Hale Group at all.","Alpha Roger’s stomach went cold.","Then the moderator again.","\"And now, please welcome the lead engineer of the Sovereign Processor Initiative, Dr. Eira Crawford.\"","Alpha Roger came forward in the chair.","Luna Margaret turned to look at what he was looking at.","Eira walked out from the left side of the stage in a dark suit, shook the director’s hand, and sat down at the head of the table. Somebody slid a folder in front of her. She opened it, checked something, and said a few words to the man on her right without looking up.","Nobody was helping her. Everyone else was waiting on her.","Luna Margaret’s mouth opened.","\"That’s Eira.\" Isabella’s voice came out wrong. \"That’s Eira?\"","Luna Margaret grabbed the remote and turned the volume up, like the sound would fix it.","\"She’s a clerk,\" Isabella said. \"She files things. She told me she works in a lab.\"","\"Doing what?\"","\"I don’t know.\" Isabella looked at her mother. \"Nobody ever asked her.\"","Alpha Roger said nothing.","Four years that girl had come to this house every other Sunday.","Four years of Luna Margaret sending her into the kitchen and Isabella asking her what she did all day and never once waiting for the answer."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118 Denial","paragraphs":["Nobody in the room moved.","\"That’s not possible.\" Luna Margaret pinched the inside of her own arm hard enough to make her eyes water.","Nothing changed. The woman was still up there, sitting at the head of the table, signing her name while Killian Sterling waited for the pen.","It was Eira.","Luna Margaret had looked at that face across her dinner table for four years. She’d sent it into the kitchen on Thanksgiving. She’d told it the fish was overcooked. She’d handed it a basket of laundry on a Sunday afternoon and gone back to her show.","\"Eira. Lead engineer.\"","She shook her head like something had gotten into it.","\"It’s supposed to be Serena. Serena is the lead engineer.\"","\"Then where is she?\" Isabella was up on the edge of the couch now, close enough to the screen to see the name cards. \"Mom, she’s not even in the room.\"","Luna Margaret turned on her husband.","\"Roger. You’ve got the wrong channel.\"","\"It’s the wrong channel,\" Isabella said. \"Dad. Check it.\"","Alpha Roger didn’t touch the remote.","\"I don’t believe it,\" Isabella said. \"I’m sorry, I don’t. Eira’s whole life was taking care of people. She doesn’t have hobbies. She doesn’t have opinions. You’re telling me she’s some kind of genius?\"","\"It’s ridiculous.\" Luna Margaret’s mouth pulled tight. \"Serena has the degrees. Serena has Dr. Winthrop behind her. That girl files paperwork in a building.\"","The ceremony was already over.","It didn’t matter what they believed. By the time Alpha Roger looked down at his phone, it was on every news app he had. Same photo on all of them. Eira and Killian Sterling, hands together, the federal seal behind them.","He kept scrolling. Industry accounts congratulating her by name. Two former directors of the program. A senator. Someone had already dug up her doctorate and posted it.","Twelve years at Stanford and after. Papers he couldn’t understand a word of.","Nobody had made her up. She’d been there the entire time.","She was the one who could have carried Alpha Sebastian’s name into that building. She was the one who could have put Hale Group in that photograph.","And Alpha Roger had signed the divorce paperwork through a lawyer without telling his son a thing about it, to clear the road for Serena Winthrop.","\"We’re done,\" he said.","Luna Margaret looked at him.","He hit his own knee with the flat of his hand. \"We are done.\"","Luna Margaret’s face went hard, because she knew exactly what he meant, and she wasn’t going to sit there and hear it.","\"Done how?\" She made her voice bright. \"So she’s accomplished. Good for her. She’s still a girl who grew up in a group home. No family. No name. No one to call. Serena has all of it. Serena is still the right fit for our son.\"","Alpha Roger didn’t answer her.","He pulled up Alpha Sebastian’s number and called. It rang out and went to voicemail. He called again and it went straight through this time, which meant the phone was off.","Then he called Serena. Off.","\"Where is your brother?\" he said.","\"They probably left early.\" Isabella dropped back into the cushions. \"He lost. He’s upset. Serena went after him. Obviously.\"","Alpha Roger set the phone face down on his knee.","Alpha Sebastian had lost bids before. He came home loud. He came home three hours late with his tie in his pocket, and he called his father from the car the whole way to explain whose fault it was.","He had never once turned his phone off.","\"Call him,\" Alpha Roger said. \"From your phone. He might pick up for you.\"","Luna Margaret dialed. It didn’t even ring. Straight to the recording.","She held the phone out toward him like he could do something about it.","Alpha Roger stood up and pulled his shirt straight. His hands weren’t quite steady.","\"I’m going out.\"","\"Out where? Roger.\"","He took his keys off the table and went.","The door shut. Luna Margaret stayed where she was with her phone in her lap and the TV still running.","\"Did we do the wrong thing?\" she said. Quietly, mostly to herself.","Isabella, who had no idea her brother’s marriage was already legally over, rolled her eyes.","\"Mom, come on. She lied. Four years, in our house.\"","\"She never actually said she wasn’t—\"","\"She let us think it. Same difference.\" Isabella pulled her knees up. \"She sat right there and let us talk. Every Sunday. You know how that looks now? She was laughing at us.\"","Luna Margaret took hold of that with both hands, because it beat the alternative.","\"Not once. Four years and she never said one word.\" Her voice found some footing. \"Because we were never family to her. That’s why.\"","\"Thank you.\"","\"That’s exactly why.\"","\"And she’s about to clean up.\" Isabella flicked a hand at the screen. \"Patents, bonuses, whatever they pay those people.\"","Luna Margaret’s face moved.","She hadn’t gotten there yet. If they’d still been married, Alpha Sebastian would’ve shared in whatever success came next.","Now it was hers, free and clear.","\"Mom.\" Isabella made a face. \"You really think she’d have shared? She’s the cheapest human being I have ever met. Four years, and what did she ever do for me? She brought me soup when I got my wisdom teeth out. Two hundred bucks of soup, and she told me the price.\"","\"She did not.\"","\"She told me where she got it, which is the same thing.\" Isabella held up two fingers. \"Serena took me to Napa with her girlfriends. Serena got me into the Rosewood thing in April. Serena texts me back in like four minutes. That’s what somebody looks like when they actually want in.\"","Luna Margaret didn’t answer, but she was nodding.","Alpha Roger liked Serena for what she could do for Alpha Sebastian. Luna Margaret liked her because she was polished, because she knew who to talk to in a room.","Isabella liked her because Isabella had been embarrassed by Eira since the first Sunday she walked in with a grocery bag.","And really, what was Eira now? A scientist. Great. Nobody’s putting a scientist on a magazine. Not one woman in Luna Margaret’s tennis group could pick that name out of a lineup. You can hand a girl every award in this country and it still won’t get anybody a Saturday table at Selby’s.","\"If she’d stayed,\" Luna Margaret said slowly, \"what were we getting out of it? A line to drop at dinner. That’s it. And she’d have been impossible to live with. You know she would. She’d have had me feeling like an idiot in my own kitchen.\"","\"So we dodged a bullet.\" Isabella shrugged. \"Honestly? Good riddance.\"","They went back and forth another few minutes and talked each other most of the way down."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119 The Double Storm","paragraphs":["They cleared him a little before midnight. No findings, no hold, go home.","\"What about Serena?\"","The agent walking him out didn’t break stride. \"Miss Winthrop’s still with us.\"","\"Meaning what.\"","\"Meaning she’s not cleared.\" He held the door. \"You’re welcome to stay and keep cooperating. Otherwise, elevator’s on your left.\"","Alpha Sebastian took the elevator.","Nine hours. Four questions in eleven costumes. He had nothing left to be polite with.","Jordan was waiting at the curb, engine idling. The Hale Pack’s Beta.","Alpha Sebastian got his phone out of the property envelope and turned it on, and it went off in his hand all the way to the car. Fourteen missed. Six from his father.","He didn’t open a single one.","\"Sterling,\" he said.","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","He’d had that at two o’clock. Nobody else had the balance sheet or the clearance to take that contract off Hale Group, and Sterling hadn’t sent a subsidiary to do his dirty work. Put the family name on the bid and walked in himself.","Losing was the easy part. The hard part started in eight hours, in a room with fifteen people who’d want it explained to them slowly.","\"Does Alpha Carter know?\"","\"Finn Carter called him at three. We’ve been at headquarters since.\" Jordan pulled into traffic. \"Comms killed two stories tonight. Nothing’s public.\"","\"But everybody in the business knows. The bid, and the other thing.\" A beat. \"You and Miss Winthrop.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked out the window.","\"He wants you at the house tonight. He said tonight, not in the morning.\"","Alpha Sebastian put two fingers on the bridge of his nose.","Then, out of nowhere, Eira.","She’d been in that building today. Sterling had dropped a file in front of half the room. Somebody would have gotten to her by now, in a hallway, with that face people make.","\"Was she there?\"","Jordan’s hands moved on the wheel. A Beta doesn’t lie to his Alpha. He can take his time, though.","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","\"Does she know?\"","There was no answering that.","\"Alpha Sebastian.\" Jordan kept his eyes on the road. \"Pull up the news. Any of it.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s phone died before the article finished loading.","He plugged it in. The screen stayed black.","Jordan caught that in the mirror and figured it was just as well. Let him take Alpha Carter’s storm first. The other thing could sit an hour.","He wasn’t sure his Alpha could take both in one night.","\"Alpha.\" Jordan kept it even. \"Alpha Carter’s not angry about the bid. He’s angry it was personal. He spent a fortune tonight and called in favors he’d been sitting on for years, and he did it burying something that had nothing to do with the company.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes moved. \"Office first. The Shaw patent proposal, it’s on my desk.\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","They swung by Hale Group for the file and were through the Carter gate by one, with the family still at the table and the estate manager standing at the end of it.","\"Alpha Sebastian is here. His Beta’s with him.\"","Finn and his sister Fiona both looked up. Something flickered across Fiona’s face before she could hide it.","Alpha Carter didn’t put his knife down. \"Conference room. They can wait.\"","Fiona opened her mouth. Her father’s eyes came up and she closed it.","\"Get a grip. That man’s mated. There was a ceremony, there’s a Luna on the Hale rolls, and even if there weren’t, his head’s been somewhere else the whole time you’ve known him. Quit throwing yourself at a bonded Alpha in front of two hundred people.\"","\"I said we could feed them.\"","\"He cost this pack nine figures today. He can skip a meal.\"","Finn pushed the roast down the table. \"Dad. Try that. It’s actually good.\"","\"Fiona. Eat.\"","It broke, barely.","\"Finish your dinner.\" Alpha Carter had come down a notch, and the pressure came off the room with it. \"And drop the Hale thing. You don’t even like him that much and we both know it. You want a pact that’s worth signing, aim at Sterling.\"","\"The Sterlings don’t need one.\" Fiona set her glass down. \"Three hundred years of their own territory and not one border they didn’t win outright. Nobody’s traded a daughter into that house since before Grandpa was born, and they’ve never needed to.\"","\"They’ve never needed to. That’s the point of them.\"","\"And I’d be doing it solo, because that man won’t let an unmated female inside ten feet of him.\"","\"That’s called discipline.\"","\"Sis, you land somebody like that, he stays landed.\" Finn shrugged. \"Sterling’s never carried a second scent in his life. Not once, not at anything, and people have looked. Half the mated females you grew up with are standing in their own front hall at midnight trying to figure out who’s on their husband’s coat.\"","She knew. She’d tried.","Two years ago, the Ridgeline benefit, four packs in one ballroom and every unmated female in the room scented up to the collarbone. She walked the whole length of it and asked Killian Sterling to dance.","Two hundred people. He didn’t even give her the courtesy of pretending to think about it.","He wasn’t interested. Both ways. Not in the dance, not in her.","She went back once more with cover, said his mother had suggested it.","That time he didn’t say no.","\"Bad knee.\" Then he stood up, crossed the whole room at a normal walking pace, and shook somebody’s hand over by the bar.","He could have lied better. He chose not to.","Alpha Sebastian Hale remembered names. He’d never once made her feel like part of the furniture. If her father hadn’t told her the man was married she’d have gone after him without blinking.","\"Worry about yourself for once. You’re almost twenty-four.\"","Finn’s whole face changed. \"I met someone.\"","His father and his sister both turned.","\"I asked you yesterday,\" Fiona said. \"You told me no.\"","\"That was yesterday.\"","Fiona put her fork down. \"You met her today?\"","Finn’s ears went red.","\"Oh my God. Dad. Look at your son.\"","The rest of dinner went easier than the start of it. Half an hour, and Alpha Carter still didn’t get up."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120 The Truth Crashes Down 1","paragraphs":["The conference room was two rooms from the dining room. Close enough to hear chairs move.","Alpha Sebastian sat with his hands folded. Somebody had refilled his water three times and nobody had spoken to him since he walked in.","He knew what this was. He’d have done the same thing. If he couldn’t sit in a room for forty minutes he had no business running Hale Group at all.","Jordan caught the movement in the hall first and stood. \"Alpha Carter’s coming.\"","Alpha Sebastian got up.","\"Alpha Carter. Finn.\"","\"Mm.\" Alpha Carter came in without offering a hand. He didn’t sit down either, and neither did his son.","Alpha Sebastian didn’t wait to be asked.","\"The contract’s on me. My personal conduct put the company in that position and I’m not going to dress it up. I’m addressing the board myself at eight.\"","\"The contract’s gone.\" Alpha Carter waved that off. \"I don’t need the speech. What’s the fix?\"","Jordan passed the folder over. Alpha Sebastian held it out with both hands, and Alpha Carter tipped his chin at Finn to take it.","\"Dr. Shaw’s patent. It’s not the Initiative, but half the industry has been circling it for two years.\"","Alpha Sebastian kept it short. \"He won’t sell. He’ll partner. If Hale Group gets that partnership, the revenue is real and the optics fix themselves.\"","Finn read the first page before he handed it to his father.","He’d wondered all year why his father kept pushing this man forward.","Most people who’d had the day Alpha Sebastian just had would still be at headquarters arguing with the comms team.","This one had walked out of a federal building at midnight with a second plan in a folder.","Alpha Carter read it through. Took his time. When he looked up, some of the cold had come off him.","\"The board’s going to want answers in the morning.\"","\"They’ll get them.\"","\"Losing a bid is business. Everybody loses bids.\" Alpha Carter set the folder down. \"Letting your personal life walk into the middle of company operations is not business. That’s yours.\"","\"It is. I let this pack down.\"","\"If you want to keep your chair, you land Dr. Shaw.\" Alpha Carter said it flatly. \"I can’t carry you past this on my own. Three seats is not the whole board.\"","\"Understood. Thank you, Alpha Carter.\"","\"How good are your odds? Dr. Shaw’s a hard man to move.\"","\"I sat with him for an hour at the spring conference and we got along.\" Alpha Sebastian didn’t inflate it. \"I’ll get him in a room. If I can’t close it, I’ll take whatever the board decides and I won’t fight it.\"","Alpha Carter’s mouth moved, almost.","\"That’s the grit I saw in you back then. Miss this one and you’re demoted. I won’t fight for you. Close it and you get your dinner after all, plus another point of equity.\"","Standard playbook. Alpha Sebastian had used it himself. He’d made it through the night. Barely.","\"Go home.\" Alpha Carter picked up the folder and handed it back. \"Your father was at your headquarters this afternoon asking your people questions. I told them to keep their mouths shut.\"","He stopped at the door.","\"Sebastian. Decide what you actually want. Your name, or a woman. Don’t let something like this come back around a second time.\"","\"Thank you, Alpha Carter.\"","--","Alpha Sebastian got out of that house in one piece, which was more than he’d expected walking in. It was ten past one.","In the car he drank half a bottle of water in three swallows and let his head go back against the seat.","His phone was charged now.","He opened the news.","Top of the page, red banner on it.","BREAKING: Sovereign Processor Initiative Awards Federal Contract to Sterling Group","He tapped it.","The photo took a second to load.","Alpha Killian Sterling and Eira, shaking hands under the federal seal, both of them turned toward the camera.","Alpha Sebastian sat forward.","It was her. There was no arguing with it. Same hair, same suit, same everything he’d seen walking out of that building this morning.","Jordan watched it land and gave it a second before he spoke.","\"Alpha. Luna Eira’s the lead engineer on the Sovereign Processor Initiative. She signed a federal nondisclosure when she came on. She couldn’t have told you, and she couldn’t have told anybody else either.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s fingers were shaking against the phone.","\"Say that again.\"","He’d heard it. Jordan knew he’d heard it. He just needed it said twice.","Jordan pulled up his own phone and forwarded a link.","\"The program office put this out at four. Feature interview, the whole team. Over a hundred thousand views by dinner.\"","He kept his voice flat, the way you do when the content is going to do the damage on its own. \"Three minute video, team bios, project timeline. Dr. Thorne has the National Medal of Science, awarded posthumously. Luna Eira has the federal science achievement award from this year. Five people get it annually. She’s the youngest recipient they’ve ever had.\"","Jordan had learned all of this at two in the afternoon and he was still not over it.","Four years of a woman who drove a car with a hundred and forty thousand miles on it and made dinner for people who didn’t thank her. And she was one of five in the country.","Alpha Sebastian had built his career on reading people. He’d hired half his executive team out from under competitors.","He’d looked at his own wife every day for four years and seen a housekeeper with a lab badge.","There was one more thing Jordan hadn’t said yet.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes hadn’t moved off the headline. He wasn’t scrolling.","\"What else. Say it.\""]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121 The Truth Crashes Down 2","paragraphs":["\"Serena Winthrop isn’t on the project roster.\" Jordan swallowed. \"Not as staff, not as a contributor, not in the acknowledgments. I don’t know if she was removed or if she was never on it.\"","Alpha Sebastian lifted his head slowly. Serena had already dropped out of his mind entirely.","\"Eira runs it,\" he said. \"Eira runs the whole thing.\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","His hand jerked. His thumb caught the link, and the phone came out of his grip and hit the floor mat face up, article open.","The still frame at the top of the video. Eira in the center, Davies on her left, Claire on her right, a black mic sitting just under her chin. Head slightly up. Looking straight into the room.","Serena had mentioned an Eira on the project once. Months ago. In passing. Just the first name, the way you’d mention weather.","He’d never once thought to ask.","\"Alpha.\" Jordan checked the mirror. \"Where to?\"","Alpha Sebastian bent down and picked up the phone.","\"My parents’.\"","The car pulled out. He watched the gate close behind them in the side mirror, and then he pressed play.","Reporter: Dr. Crawford, how long have you been on this project?","Eira: Seven years. It was my mentor’s program. I came on as a graduate student and I never worked on anything else. When he died four years ago the program went dormant. When it restarted, I took it over.","So that was what she’d meant. I lost my job.","She’d told him that at a dinner table. He remembered thinking he’d have to ask his father about finding her something.","Reporter: You’re young to be running a federal program. Was there ever a point you thought it was too much?","Alpha Sebastian stopped breathing.","Eira: Yes. But nobody understood the architecture better than I did. So it was going to be me or it was going to be nobody.","Reporter: What kept you going?","Eira: Something my mentor said. He told me that as long as we’re buying our processors from somewhere else, somebody else decides what we’re allowed to build. He said the country doesn’t own anything it can’t make. I’ve thought about that every day for seven years.","Applause off camera.","Alpha Sebastian had lived with that woman for four years and never heard her say anything that weighed a pound. He’d assumed there was nothing there to say.","He kept watching.","At the end, the questions went personal.","Reporter: You’re twenty-five, and you’ve given all of it to this work. Any plans to settle down? Take a mate?","Alpha Sebastian held his breath.","Eira: No.","His face emptied.","Reporter: Not the marrying type, or just not yet?","Eira: I’m going to pass on that one.","Reporter: Fair enough. Thank you, Dr. Crawford.","The video ended and went black, and his own face was in it.","Alpha Sebastian sat there.","\"Jordan.\" His voice came out wrong. \"She sat in front of a federal camera and said no.\"","Jordan didn’t answer.","Alpha Sebastian forwarded the article to her with one line under it.","[Why did you tell them you’re not mated?]","Sent.","Then, under it, gray text.","Not Delivered.","He opened the thread. Red circle with an exclamation point sitting next to the link.","He tapped it. Tried again. Same thing.","He called her.","It didn’t ring. It went straight to a recording. The person you’re trying to reach is not accepting calls at this time.","He sat with the phone against his ear until the line went dead.","His jaw locked. \"Jordan. You call her.\"","Jordan dialed and put it on speaker. Same recording, same three seconds in.","\"She’s got me too, Alpha.\"","Alpha Sebastian didn’t answer. The car got colder anyway, and Jordan cracked his window an inch without being obvious about it.","Jordan gave it a careful beat. \"She’d have seen the file Sterling handed out. About you and Miss Winthrop. That’s probably what the block is—\"","\"I know what the block is.\"","Jordan shut his mouth.","The man had lost a federal contract nine hours ago and taken it standing up. Two blocked numbers and he was coming apart in the back seat.","\"Change of plans. The Thorne estate.\"","Jordan didn’t ask whether this was a reasonable hour for an unannounced visit. He turned the car around.","The Thorne estate was dark when they pulled up. Every window. No car in the drive, porch light off, and two days of mail sitting in the box.","Alpha Sebastian got out anyway and went up the walk.","He got about four feet from the door and stopped, because there was nothing there. Whatever scent she’d left on that porch was days cold and had rain over it. The house had been shut since the weekend.","He stood there a minute in a dead man’s driveway with his hands in his pockets.","Then it hit him, all at once and from a strange angle.","He didn’t know where else to look.","Not one other address. He didn’t know if she had friends. He didn’t know where she went on the Sundays she wasn’t at his mother’s table. Four years, and this house was the only place he could name.","She’d never gone anywhere before. She’d always just been where he left her.","--","Ten minutes later, they were back on the road.","Neither of them said a word.","By the time they reached the Hale estate, it was a little before two. The downstairs lights were still on, all of them, which never happened.","The front door was unlocked. He got two steps into the entry before he heard his mother in the sitting room, low and fast, the way she talked when she was scared.","\"So what do we tell him? The severance already went through. It’s on the pack registry, Roger.\""]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122 Too Late to Hide the Truth","paragraphs":["This time he heard it clearly.","Dissolution certificates.","He came around the corner with his coat still on, frowning. \"What dissolution certificates?\"","Luna Margaret’s mouth shut. She wouldn’t look at him.","Alpha Roger cut a look sideways at his wife that said everything about what he thought of her volume control.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw set. \"Last time it was bonding certificates. Now it’s dissolution certificates. Somebody tell me what’s going on in this house.\"","Luna Margaret looked at her husband. He knew what she was asking without a word.","They had to tell him. Eventually. The Mate Bond Dissolution Certificates had already been issued. There was no hiding that forever.","Just not tonight. Maybe in a day or two. When he’d had time to breathe.","Alpha Roger looked at what nine hours in that building had carved into his son’s face.","\"The one I told you,\" he said. \"There’s no thirty year ceremony. The Elders aren’t hosting anything. I said that because your mother was standing right there and I wasn’t going to do it in a hallway.\"","Luna Margaret’s head came up.","He’s using that?","\"Your mother and I filed. That’s what she’s talking about.\"","Alpha Sebastian stopped where he stood. He’d lost count of how many times today somebody had said a sentence he had to hear twice.","\"What?\"","\"We went down to the registry. It wasn’t for anything to celebrate.\" Alpha Roger’s face didn’t move. \"We were filing.\"","Luna Margaret sat very still with her heart going. You don’t say that out loud. Not in this house, not as a joke. Every older female she knew would have told him the same thing.","But she’d never won an argument with her husband in thirty years, and in this house he made the calls.","Alpha Sebastian didn’t buy it. \"That was a few days ago. There’s no way you’d have certificates yet.\"","\"We don’t have them. We’re in the cooling-off period.\" Alpha Roger didn’t blink once. \"Your mother’s been trying to work out how to tell you when it’s over. That’s what you walked in on. Why we got here is between the two of us.\"","\"You told me you were solid.\"","\"I told you a lot of things that week.\"","Alpha Sebastian let out a long breath through his nose. The exhaustion was all over him.","Luna Margaret got there fast. \"Nothing’s decided. We’re taking the time, that’s all. That’s what the period is for.\"","Alpha Sebastian sat down on the couch and looked at the floor.","\"You two work it out. I’m getting in the shower.\"","--","When he came out, his parents were still sitting on the couch waiting for him.","They wanted to hear about today. He could see it on them.","Alpha Sebastian sat down and took a handful of crackers off the tray, ate them without tasting anything.","If Eira were here there’d have been a plate. She’d never once let him come home to nothing.","Then he remembered she’d blocked him and he didn’t know what city she was sleeping in, and the rest of it went dry in his mouth.","\"Dad. Mom. One of you call Eira.\"","Luna Margaret’s forehead creased. \"Why would I be calling her?\"","Alpha Sebastian took a second with it.","\"Sterling used me and Serena to blow up the bid this afternoon. He did it in front of the room. Eira was in that building. Whatever’s going around, she’s heard it by now, and she’s not answering me.\"","Alpha Roger leaned forward. \"You know who she is now.\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded. \"I knew she worked for Thorne. I didn’t know she was cleared at that level.\"","Luna Margaret set her cup down hard. \"She let us think she was nobody. Four years. Serena’s in the same field and she never made a mystery out of herself.\"","\"No,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"She sure didn’t.\"","His mother took that for agreement and kept going. He let her get two sentences out.","\"Mom. Listen to what you just said. Serena told us everything. Which program,whose name was on it. At your table, on a Sunday, with the staff walking in and out.\"","\"I don’t see what—\"","\"Serena was never read into that program. Eira was.\" He put his glass down. \"Eira signed a federal nondisclosure her first week. That’s why we never got a word out of her. She wasn’t playing games with this family. She was staying out of prison.\"","\"Sebastian—\"","\"The Bureau picked us both up this morning.\"","Luna Margaret went still.","\"Nine hours. Two agents, no windows. \" He rubbed his eyes. \"Serena’s still in there. They brought in Dr. Winthrop too.\"","She got halfway off the couch. \"Did you have counsel with you? Tell me you didn’t sit in a federal interview alone.\"","\"I had counsel.\"","\"Thank the Moon.\" Then her face reorganized itself. \"What was that girl thinking, dragging you into her mess?\"","Alpha Sebastian let it go. Two months ago Serena started bringing him things she had no business having, and his mother had called her ambitious. Said it twice at that same table.","He looked at his father. \"That’s what cost us the contract.\"","\"Nobody hands a federal award to your competition over a girlfriend.\" Alpha Roger’s brow came down. \"What am I missing?\"","Then he remembered the name his son had said thirty seconds ago and answered himself.","\"Alpha Sterling.\"","\"I underestimated him.\" Alpha Sebastian was already back on the only thing his head wanted. \"Dad. Call her.\"","Alpha Roger dialed. It never rang. Recording, then dead air.","Luna Margaret tried. Same three seconds, same voice.","Alpha Sebastian opened his mouth to say Isabella should try, and his father beat him to it.\"Don’t bother putting Isabella on it. She’s blocked all of us.\"","Alpha Sebastian heard the shape of that sentence and never caught what was wrong with it.","Normally he’d have caught it. Tonight, it slid right past him.","\"She’s angry at me. Why would she block you?\"","Neither of them answered.","Two weeks ago Luna Margaret would have been on her feet over that. Alpha Roger would have told him a man who can’t keep order in his own house has no business running one for four hundred people.","They sat there.","He was too far gone to hear it.","\"Tomorrow, after the company, I’ll go find her.\"","\"And Serena?\" Luna Margaret said. \"You’re going to let that girl sit in a federal building all night with nobody in her corner?\"","Serena was the one door still open, and she meant to keep walking him toward it.","\"Jordan’s got it. Gallagher’s office has somebody on the way.\"","Alpha Roger had gone the other direction entirely.\"Let the Winthrops handle their own. They’ve got more pull downtown than we do.\" He said it evenly. \"Tomorrow you go find Eira. And don’t send anybody to do it for you.\"","\"First minute I’m free.\"","\"Good.\" Alpha Roger clapped him on the shoulder, stood, and gave his wife a look.\"Upstairs.\""]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123 She Always Does","paragraphs":["The bedroom door hadn’t finished closing.","\"What was that?\" Luna Margaret got most of a shout into a whisper. \"You still want her back in this family? It’s done. It’s filed. The Winthrops have a seat at every table in this territory. What does Eira have?\"","Alpha Roger pulled his tie loose.","\"A federal contract, a medal.\"","\"She’s wolfless, Roger. She grew up in an Omega home. She can’t scent a room, she’s got no bloodline, she’s got nothing to put on a form.\"","\"And she has a face that opens a federal building.\" He hung the tie up. \"Mine doesn’t. Yours doesn’t. Sebastian’s doesn’t. Hers does.\"","Luna Margaret stopped.","\"You didn’t watch the interview.\"","She didn’t answer.","\"That certificate isn’t a prize. It’s a door.\" He sat down on the end of the bed. \"Whoever partners with her on the follow-on work goes straight into the federal defense chain. Not as a vendor. Inside it.\"","\"Then we buy in. We have the money.\"","\"There’s nothing to buy. She picks the partner.\" He looked at the carpet. \"Sterling’s name went next to hers at four o’clock.\"","Luna Margaret’s mouth closed.","\"Four years she ran this pack. Every funeral, every dispute, every ledger, every elder who called the house at midnight. On nothing.\" He said it slowly. \"And the whole time she was holding the only key to the room we’ve been trying to get into since my father had this house.\"","\"She never said one word.\"","\"She wasn’t allowed to.\" Alpha Roger’s voice went flat. \"And I’d bet the house she was going to hand it to Sebastian anyway. That’s what all of it was for.\"","Luna Margaret sat down on her side of the bed.","She followed the math fine. She just couldn’t get her throat around being sweet to that girl. Four years of holding her nose, and now she was supposed to pour the tea.","\"Alpha Sterling already has her.\"","\"Alpha Sterling has one contract. Sebastian has four years.\" Alpha Roger pulled his shoes off. \"The boy apologizes, she comes back. She always does.\"","\"You think it’s that easy?\"","\"She’s never once asked us for anything.\" He turned off the lamp. \"Go to sleep.\"","--","While Alpha Sebastian and Serena spent the night coming apart, Eira slept like a rock.","Best eight hours she’d had in a month.","Alpha Sebastian, blocked. His parents, blocked. His sister, blocked. As of four o’clock yesterday afternoon she was done with the Hales, and she was done with him.","Serena was sitting in federal custody. Davies wouldn’t have to step aside for her after all. Her name was off the roster, and years of everybody’s work wasn’t getting handed to somebody who hadn’t earned a line of it.","Everything landed right where it was supposed to.","She slept straight through it.","Sun came across the bed sometime after nine.","Eira stretched, took her sweet time getting up, brushed her teeth, washed her face, and made herself a real breakfast instead of drinking coffee over the sink like a person with somewhere to be.","Then she decided to do absolutely nothing.","She threw on a shirt three sizes too big, dragged the couch over to the window, and put the cardboard box on the floor next to it. Letters and drawings from the kids at the Omega home. She’d been saving them for a day like this.","She stretched out and her back hit something hard.","Her phone. She’d put it on Do Not Disturb before bed and buried it under a cushion.","The second she flipped that off, the thing lost its mind. Buzzed so hard she almost dropped it. Notifications came pouring down the screen and just kept coming.","Miss Gwen was pinned at the top. Eira called her back first.","Miss Gwen had seen it. She’d rounded up the whole house in the common room to watch it together.","Eira let her talk and went through the drawings while she did. Crooked handwriting. A pinecone wind chime somebody had put together with way too much glue.","\"Miss Gwen.\" Her voice shifted a little. \"Turn down the year end donation from Hale Group this year.\"","Silence on the other end.","\"I’m funding the home myself from here on out.\"","\"Honey, that award money is yours. You hang onto it.\"","\"It’s not just the award. Licensing on the pre award patents comes to me. That’s the bigger number.\"","Miss Gwen’s voice went serious. \"You sure about this?\"","\"Dead sure.\"","They talked a while longer before they hung up.","Then Eira went back to her messages.","The loudest by far was the Sterling Group chat.","It had gone off like a car alarm the second the interview posted and apparently never quit.","Eira: what’d I miss","Natalie: MA’AM","Natalie: MA’AM.","Kate: my mother called me. my actual mother. she saw the segment and asked if I’d ever met you. I said I sit eight feet from you. she hung up on me","Natalie: there was a FEDERAL SEAL behind you. an actual seal. on the wall","Kate: and you came into the office monday and asked me where the good stapler was","Eira: it’s a good stapler","Eira: and it’s Eira. don’t you people have jobs","Kate: not today we don’t","Miles: Mr. Sterling is in an outstanding mood. Bonuses hit at ten.","Natalie: I checked twice. then I logged out and checked again","Kate: I’m getting the tires done. I’m finally getting the tires done","Miles: Dr. Crawford, we’re putting together a celebration dinner. We’d like your whole team there. Does that work?","Eira: let me run it by them","Miles: Appreciate it. If they’re in, I’ll bring the invitations over myself.","Kate: I volunteer as tribute","Natalie: SAME","Kate: Miles I have a car. Miles the car has new tires","She ran it by the team. All eleven of them were in inside of four minutes. Davies sent back a thumbs up and then, thirty seconds later, a second thumbs up.","Eira: Number Nine, Southridge Estates. Drop them there and I’ll hand them out.","The three dots came up in the chat. Sat there a while. Went away.","--","Back at Sterling Group, Natalie and Kate spun around in their chairs at the same time and gave Miles the puppy eyes. They hadn’t gotten to tag along yesterday. Surely today.","Miles shook his head before either of them got a word out.","\"Number Nine, Southridge,\" he said, \"is not a delivery any of us are making.\""]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124 The Visit","paragraphs":["Eira had the pinecone wind chime in her hand when the doorbell went off.","Lila was on the screen with her arms crossed, staring straight into the camera like it had personally wronged her.","Eira blinked at it.","Lila was the only person she knew who hadn’t sent her anything since yesterday. Not last night, not this morning. Not one word.","She opened the door.","Lila stood there and gave her a look that was somehow furious and not furious at all. Her eyes went in a full circle. Then her whole face broke open.","\"Oh my GOD.\"","She got both arms around Eira and squeezed hard enough to lift her off her heels.","Eira couldn’t breathe. She was smiling anyway.","\"I thought you were mad at me,\" she said when she got loose. \"You didn’t answer anything I sent.\"","\"Do not get me started.\" Lila waved that off and went straight for the couch like she lived there. \"That’s Professor Chase. I was two hours deep into reading every single article written about you, having the time of my life, and he pulls me into the lab. I got out forty minutes ago. I came here first. I haven’t even eaten.\"","Eira sat down next to her and handed her a juice box.","Lila drank the whole thing in one go and turned around with her eyes lit up.","\"Okay. I knew you were smart the day I met you. You read my thesis like it was a menu.\" She waved the empty box around. \"But this? My entire family lost their minds. And I mean the whole pack.\"","Eira smiled a little. \"You’re exaggerating.\"","\"I am absolutely not. \" Lila dropped back into the cushions. \"Oh, and I heard something. Your ex and that Serena woman both got picked up yesterday. Is that real? Because if it is, somebody is sitting on it hard. There’s nothing out there. Not a word.\"","\"It’s real.\" Eira nodded. \"Sebastian got cleared and sent home. Serena didn’t.\"","Anything that touched the Initiative came to her the same hour it happened. That update had come in around ten.","Serena had met with her attorney at eight.","--","Vincent Crawford walked into the field office at eight with a leather briefcase and the same face he wore into every room. Calm. Unhurried. Like he’d already read the last page.","They gave him a private room with Serena.","Anybody who followed either world knew the name.","Crawford Pack was one of the four first tier packs on the continent, and Vincent was the current Alpha’s son.","He could have taken a seat on that council at twenty-two and never worked a day in his life.","Instead he went to law school, then qualified in both systems—human and Council—which maybe three attorneys in the country had ever bothered to do.","Fourteen years in and he’d never lost one that went to trial. Human juries liked him. Council tribunals respected him, which was rarer and worth more. When a pack got into something it couldn’t buy its way out of, somebody in the room always said the same thing.","Call Crawford.","He hadn’t taken a case for the money in years. He took the ones he wanted.","And he’d been on a plane six hours after Serena called him.","Twenty-three hours had taken the polish off her. Her hair hung flat. Her eyes were red at the rims.","The second she saw him her face came apart.","\"Vincent.\" Her voice shook. \"I didn’t think you’d actually come.\"","\"You called me. Of course I came.\"","--","They’d met in Prague four years back.","A guy at the bar dropped something in Vincent’s drink. Serena caught it and said it in Spanish, low and fast, right as he reached for the glass. The guy didn’t speak Spanish. He just kept smiling and kept holding it out.","Vincent’s face went cold half a second later.","When the guy put it together he called her something ugly and threw the drink. Vincent got an arm up and wore it instead.","They traded numbers that night. He took her to dinner to say thanks. They had a week.","Then Alpha Sebastian flew out for her birthday and she took the call standing three feet from Vincent.","\"Boyfriend?\" he asked, careful about it.","And she knew right then.","\"Take a guess.\"","He backed off after that. Kept his distance and kept in touch. Something showed up every holiday, never flashy, always something he’d thought about.","She was glad she never chased him. Lawyers are careful people.","But she never let the line go slack. You don’t cut a rope like that.","--","\"Vincent, I didn’t do this.\" Her voice broke. \"I would never leak classified material. Not in a million years.\"","\"Okay.\" He laid the briefcase flat and opened a legal pad. \"Start at the top. Don’t clean anything up for me. The parts you think make you look bad are the parts I need first.\"","She walked him through it. Every week since she’d come onto the Sovereign Processor Initiative. Cut out of meetings. Left off the distribution lists. Handed work you’d give a first year grad student and no one to complain to.","\"And the video.\" Her hands wouldn’t hold still. \"I know how it looks. But somebody asks me one basic question about my own project and I can’t answer it? On my own team? I should know something.\"","The pen stopped.","\"Did you ever have access to the data?\"","\"No.\" Her mouth went tight. \"I told you back in the spring. Eira’s had me locked out since day one and the whole team takes their cues from her.\"","He wrote that down and let it sit.","\"Then why would Dr. Crawford flag you as a leak risk to begin with?\" His voice stayed level. His eyes didn’t. \"Does she know about you and Sebastian Hale?\"","There it was.","\"I swear to you I didn’t know he was mated when we picked things back up.\"","Vincent’s head came up.","He’d known who Eira Crawford was since the plane. Everybody with a phone did by now. Lead engineer, twenty five, federal medal. Nobody had bothered to mention she was married to Alpha Sebastian Hale.","\"Sebastian Hale is mated to Eira Crawford. And you’re seeing him.\"","\"I’m not seeing him.\" Fast. \"We were together when we were kids. I went abroad, we ended it, and while I was gone he married her out of nowhere. I didn’t find out until the day of the presentation.\"","He didn’t write that one down.","\"She knew about me the entire time. I didn’t know about her.\" Serena leaned in, eyes wet. \"Not until it was already too late.\"","He was quiet a beat.","\"Hale lied to you.\"","A tear went down her cheek. He slid the tissue box across.","\"Thank you. For coming.\"","She didn’t say yes. She didn’t say no. She let the quiet do it for her.","Then she switched tracks.","\"You should know Eira has a relationship with Killian Sterling. During the blackout period she spent a month working as his personal assistant. Ask anybody at Sterling Group, they all know her.\"","The pen started moving again.","\"So your position is that Alpha Sterling and Dr. Crawford put this together between them. He takes out a competitor’s bid. She takes out the woman sleeping with her husband.\"","Serena nodded. No hesitation at all. Her eyes were still red but her voice had gone level.","\"Yes.\"","Vincent looked at her for a long moment.","Then he closed the notebook.","\"I’ll get you out of here,\" he said. \"You have my word on that.\""]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125 The Legal Strategy","paragraphs":["\"All you did was ask to see your own project’s data,\" Vincent said. \"You’re on the team. That’s not a crime by itself. Unless they can show you pulled it off the system or handed it to somebody outside, they don’t have a case worth filing.\"","He stood and buttoned his jacket.","\"Intent is a story. Transfer is a record. They’ve got no record.\"","Serena caught it right away.","To charge her they needed the act. All they had was what they thought was going on in her head, and nobody can put that in an evidence bag.","\"What happens now?\"","\"They have to put you in front of a magistrate. That’s tomorrow morning at the latest. I’ll be there.\" He picked up the briefcase. \"Between now and then I’m talking to Sebastian Hale, and I’m pulling everything there is on Killian Sterling and Eira Crawford.\"","He turned for the door.","\"Vincent. Wait.\"","He looked back.","\"Sebastian and I.\" She stopped. Her voice went thin. \"It wasn’t his fault. I knew exactly what I was doing. Don’t put this on him.\"","Vincent stood there a second.","\"Serena. There are other men in this country.\" He said it quietly. \"You don’t have to keep doing this to yourself.\"","Her eyes filled up.","\"Vincent—\"","He nodded once and walked out.","-- -","Eira looked at the name on her screen. Vincent Crawford.","She typed it into a tab. Firm bio first, then about forty articles. Photos. Bar admissions in two systems. A case list long enough that she quit scrolling.","She looked at his face a while. Something moved in her chest and went quiet again before she could name it.","\"Crawford’s golden boy.\" Lila was reading over her shoulder. \"That’s who she got? How?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"My mom is going to lose it.\" Lila dropped onto the couch and put her feet up. \"Her family’s territory runs right up against Crawford’s. Her father and Henry’s father signed the border treaty back in the day, so the two of them got shipped to all the same things. Joint runs, treaty dinners, that summer program the Council runs for heirs. Two Alpha kids stuck at the same kids’ table for fifteen years.\"","Eira turned the letter over in her hands and said nothing.","\"They were close. Then she mated my dad and moved out to Sterling territory, and you know how that goes. Two thousand miles, two different packs. It just stopped.\" Lila shrugged. \"Henry found his Luna a couple years later and took over Crawford.\"","\"Mm.\"","\"You know what nobody prints, though?\" Lila said. \"Something happened in that family when Vincent was five or six. Big. Whatever it was, it broke Clara.\"","Eira’s thumb stopped moving on the paper.","\"Henry stepped back from the Alpha seat for a while. His father took the pack again and the Beta ran the day to day. My grandfather covered a lot of it too, borders, arbitration, all of it.\" Lila made a face. \"My mom still won’t say a word about what happened, and my mom will say anything about anybody.\"","\"How long was he out?\"","\"Couple years? Then Lainey came. Born in the middle of a blizzard, which is a whole thing at Thanksgiving.\" Lila’s voice lifted. \"Clara got a lot better after that. That’s when Henry came back.\"","Quiet for a second.","\"Lainey shoots for magazines now. She’s good.\"","\"How old.\"","\"Twenty three, twenty four?\" Lila looked over. \"Why?\"","\"No reason.\"","Lila caught her face changing and swung the wheel hard.","\"Okay, I know you have negative free time, but any chance you’d look at my companion bot? I’m dead in the water on the main controller.\"","\"Killian said you were coming into R and D. We just signed with Sterling.\"","\"That’s the recon platform. Forty pounds and ugly.\" Lila waved it off. \"Mine’s small. Domestic. About ten times smarter than anything on a shelf right now.\"","\"I’ll look,\" Eira said. \"Robotics isn’t my field. You’ll need four or five chips in that thing and I can help with two.\"","\"YES.\" Lila got both arms around her. \"Going on record. My brother does not deserve you.\"","Eira went still. \"What?\"","\"Nothing.\" Lila let go, grinning. \"Ignore me.\"","They spent the rest of the afternoon talking and laughing.","Alpha Sebastian spent his getting taken apart.","The Hale Group board first thing, two hours of it. Then the Carter shareholders, who came in smiling and left without shaking anybody’s hand. Then his own executive team, who were more scared than angry, which was worse.","By five thirty he sat down in his own chair and felt like somebody had reached in and pulled his spine out through his back.","Jordan set a glass of water on the desk.","\"Ms. Winthrop was released about an hour ago. No charges filed. She’s still under investigation.\"","\"And the attorney?\" Alpha Sebastian pressed the bridge of his nose and drank half the glass.","\"She brought in her own. Vincent Crawford. He’s downstairs. He’d like fifteen minutes.\"","Alpha Sebastian knew the name. Everybody knew the name.","\"He wants to see me?\"","\"Whether she gets charged comes down mostly to what you say. His words.\"","Alpha Sebastian had seen that coming since yesterday. He nodded. \"Send him up.\"","Jordan called the front desk.","Downstairs, the receptionist handed Vincent a key card. \"Top floor, sir.\"","He stepped into the elevator.","His phone went off as the doors opened.","Associate: Mr. Crawford, Hale and Dr. Crawford dissolved their mate bond. Filing went final last week.","Vincent stopped with one foot out of the car.","[So Hale had actually done it. For Serena.]","And the dates said he’d done it before the broadcast. Before anybody in the country knew who Eira Crawford was.","\"Mr. Crawford?\" Jordan was in the hall. \"Right this way.\"","Vincent put the phone away and followed him in.","The two men Serena had wrapped her life around finally stood in the same room.","\"Vincent Crawford.\"","\"Sebastian Hale.\"","One handshake. Short.","Vincent didn’t sit down first and didn’t waste anything.","\"One question. Did Serena Winthrop ever talk to you about project data?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at him a long time.","Vincent held it. \"You can talk to me, Mr. Hale. She did something for me once. I owe her, and she knows it.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw moved.","But he answered.","\"She brought it up. I shut it down.\"","\"Brought it up.\" Vincent’s eyes came up off the pad.","Alpha Sebastian got it. \"No. She didn’t.\"","\"Good.\" Vincent’s voice dropped. \"Hold onto that. Serena Winthrop never said one word to you about that program. Not on a call, not over dinner, not in a text at two in the morning. If it’s in writing somewhere, I need to know tonight and not from an agent.\"","\"It isn’t.\"","They went another twenty minutes. What the Bureau already had, what they’d come asking for next, where Alpha Sebastian was exposed and where he wasn’t.","Alpha Sebastian checked his watch three times.","Vincent noticed the third one.","\"Somewhere you need to be?\"","\"Yeah.\" Alpha Sebastian’s mouth pulled tight. \"I have to find somebody.\"","\"Serena?\"","\"No.\" He stopped a second. \"My wife. Eira.\"","Vincent closed the pad.","\"Mr. Hale, I read the filing on the way up.\" He said it evenly. \"She isn’t your wife.\""]}]);
